eady threaded AES-CTR/zlib + forked per-set pool). Answers unchanged; full solver-test 31/31 pass.\n\n## Proposed lib additions\n- `lib.common.fast_aes_unzip(data, passwords)` -> [(name, Future[bytes])] + sha256 cache: the `_aes_member` / `_fast_unzip` pair in day09 binary-nimble solve.py (WinZip AE-x without pyzipper's pure-Python HMAC pass; zlib/pycryptodome/hashlib release the GIL so members inflate in parallel). Every lane whose evidence.zip carries a large member benefits.\nVARIANT AXIS: (speed cycle, no answer change) the \"8.21s on single_solve\" flag was CPU contention from parallel solver-tests, not the solver: isolated it runs 0.55-0.60 s wall on the single (taskset 2 vCPUs, ~0.75 s CPU) and 1.2 s on a 3-set Mastery; critical path is the d08 67 MB Swift member's AES-CTR||inflate||sha256 pipeline (done at ~0.37 s) + ~0.09 s of field analysis -- measure with `taskset -c 0,1 /usr/bin/time python3 solve.py ...`, not under a loaded solver-test.\n\nVARIANT AXIS: (speed cycle, no code change, D14) the \"4.11 s on single_solve\" flag was measured under load (load avg ~4.5) -- isolated and pinned to 2 CPUs: single 0.51 s wall (0.6 s unpinned; the harness cProfile itself shows 0.048 s for import), 5-set Mastery auto-mastery-7439276e 1.42 s wall pinned / 0.80 s unpinned; all 21 cases pass with every answer_id filled. Nothing to trim that the earlier cycles have not already trimmed.\n\nVARIANT AXIS: (speed cycle, no code change, D15) the \"4.84 s on single_solve\" flag was measured under load (load avg ~6.6, harness cProfile counted 1.1 s of imports and 2.9 s of thread waits) -- isolated and pinned to 2 CPUs: single 0.90 s wall (critical path = AES-CTR+inflate of the 67 MB d08 member ~0.2 s, HCFG scans 0.09 s, capstone import 0.07 s), 5-set Mastery auto-mastery-546ae191 2.6 s pinned / 1.4 s unpinned; all 23 cases pass with every answer_id filled (solver-test single 1.26 s under concurrent load).\n\n## D17 (decoder-ring) single\n- New re-asked earlier-day fields (all G