hreads); full suite passes, Mastery 0.6-2.6 s. d20_analysis_hcfg_resource_size = RS20 u32le @ magic+8 (380 on the single, matches expected).\n\nVARIANT AXIS: (speed cycle, no code change, D21) the \"4.46 s on single_solve\" flag was measured under load (load avg ~7-12; harness cProfile of the same case totals 1.83 s, mostly thread waits on the AES/inflate pool + 0.39 s imports) -- isolated: solve.py 0.60-0.70 s wall unpinned, 0.93-1.1 s pinned to 2 CPUs on the 252-id single (252/252 match expected); no hot spot in tottime (threaded zlib inflate 0.26 s, hcfg scans 0.1 s, AES-CTR 0.09 s). Full suite 45/45 green, slowest 5-set Mastery 2.3 s inside the loaded concurrent solver-test. Nothing new to trim; the d21 loader/plugin (.cmxs) analysis adds no measurable cost.\n\nVARIANT AXIS: (speed cycle, no code change, D22) the \"3.47 s on single_solve\" flag was measured under load (load avg ~6-7.5; harness cProfile of the same case totals 1.9 s, mostly thread waits on the AES/inflate pool + imports) -- isolated: solve.py 0.60 s wall unpinned, 1.0 s pinned to 2 CPUs, 1.0-1.5 s on 1 CPU, on the 264-id single (264/264 match expected). No hot spot: hcfg() scans total 0.07 s (0.06 s is the 67 MB d08 member; the 5.7 MB bundled d22--FSharp.Core.dll scan is ~2 ms). FSharp.Core cannot be skipped: d22_artifact_sha256_3 is its sha256, and its decrypt is ~30 ms in a pool thread off the d08 critical path. Full suite 47/47 green, slowest case 2.7 s inside the loaded concurrent solver-test.\n\nVARIANT AXIS: (speed cycle, no code change, D23) the \"4.55 s on single_solve\" flag was measured under load (load avg 8-15 from parallel workers; the harness cProfile totals 2.8 s, mostly thread waits on the AES/inflate pool + ~0.5 s imports) -- measured here at load ~8: solve.py 1.2 s wall unpinned / 1.3 s pinned to 2 CPUs on the 276-id single (276/276 match expected); tottime shows no hot spot (threaded zlib inflate 0.24 s, hcfg scans 0.09 s, sha256 0.08 s, the d23 VB.NET overlay HCFG adds nothing