nswer from the PRIMARY .dll, FSharp.Core/System.* = support members)\n237\t  cffaedfe/cefaedfe Mach-O thin; cafebabe + small u32 nfat => Mach-O FAT (NOT a Java class) ; format word presumed `macho`\n238\t  504b0304 zip/jar/apk (keep nested jars whole) ; 1b4c7561 Lua ; 1b4c4a LuaJIT ; FOR1..BEAM Erlang ; 4243c0de LLVM bitcode\n239\t    jar = `jar` for Java D6/Kotlin D7/Scala D24; Scala: Main-Class is a forwarder, logic + base64 HCFG ldc in `Foo$.class` (MODULE$)\n240\t  4e454b4f 'NEKO' => Neko VM bytecode: format `neko_bytecode` (in the GM enum since D19; unseen)\n241\t  0061736d \\0asm WASM (D16): format `wasm`, architecture `wasm32` (GM-confirmed); lib.binary.wasm_layout -> sections, memories,\n242\t    data_segments (file_offset + mem_offset); wasm-objdump -x F ; HCFG RAW in data seg 0 -> raw scan finds it (crc-gate)\n243\t  ':10' text lines => Intel HEX ; 'S0'/'S1' => S-record ; no magic + ARM vector table => raw firmware (rizin -m base)\n244\tSTEP 2  rz-bin -I F   (or readelf -hlSW F)  -> lang, machine, bits, endian, static, stripped, pic, relro, nx, canary\n245\t  e_machine: 3 x86 | 62 x86-64 | 40 ARM | 183 AArch64 | 8 MIPS | 20 PPC | 21 PPC64 | 243 RISC-V | 2/43 SPARC\n246\t  labels: GM-confirmed x86-64/x86/AArch64/ARM (ELF), i386/x86-64 (PE); others = readelf spelling first, then EM_ name minus\n247\t  prefix; kind:integer => decimal e_machine. Dispatch on answer_format.kind, never on field name.\n248\t  no .symtab => stripped (answer [] / none / false); no INTERP => static; ET_DYN+INTERP => PIE; ET_REL => object file\n249\t  UPX0/UPX1 sections or \"UPX!\" or entropy>7.2 => PACKED: upx -t F; cp F /tmp/x; upx -d /tmp/x (fix zeroed UPX! first)\n250\tSTEP 3  strings -a -n6 F | grep -m8 -E 'GCC:|clang|rustc|go1\\.|GHC |OCaml|caml_|FPC |Crystal|zig|GNAT Version|gfortran|DMD|Nim|\n251\t        swift|_kDart|kfun:|__svm|MEI|nuitka|AU3!|Borland|MSVBVM|libcob|UPX|HCFG|SENGR'   -> toolchain + blob form\n252\t  toolchain -> tool: Go GoReSym -t -d -p | Rust rustfilt | .NET ilspycmd | jar javap -v -p / jadx | Swift swift-demangle\n253\t  Nim nim-demangle | PyInstaller pyinstxtractor+pycdc | AutoIt autoit-ripper | anything else: rizin -q -c 'aaa;afl' /\n254\t  analyzeHeadless (lib.binary.ghidra_decompile) | foreign arch: rizin -a <arch> / llvm-objdump-18 / Ghidra (no exec, qemu absent)\n255\tHCFG (every new member since D2)\n256\t  python: from lib.binary import hcfg_find, hcfg_scan; hcfg_find(open(F,'rb').read())  -> config, offset, encoding, key, crc_ok\n257\t  raw magic 'HCFG' | b64 'SENGR' | hex '48434647' | rot13 'FRATE' | b64-zlib 'eJ' | b64-gzip 'H4sI' -> covered by hcfg_scan\n258\t  accept only crc32(plain)==header crc AND JSON parses; keep scanning past decoys (D9 had two raw-magic decoys)\n259\t  ALWAYS check the tail: image_end = e_shoff+e_shnum*e_shentsize (or max section/segment end; PE: pefile overlay start);\n260\t  len > image_end => OVERLAY with a day magic (PK19 D19 packed; RS20 D20 = raw HCFG @+48 + scratch, res_len u32@8,\n261\t  scratch_len u16@12, sha256(scratch)@16). o = data.rfind(magic) (\"final\"); parse EVERY header field the QUESTION lists into\n262\t  a dict (size ids = that field, e.g. hcfg_resource_size = u32@8); verify its bounds/sha256; run its transform (D19\n263\t  ror8(b^k2,3)^k1); HCFG at the stated offset. overlay_offset = o, overlay_size = len(data)-o.\n264\t  NOT FOUND => hidden elsewhere: (1) packed? unpack; (2) AES S-box 637c777b / TEA 9e3779b9 / 'expand 32-byte k' => find key+IV\n265\t  near the call, decrypt with pycryptodome; (3) runs of mov [rbp-x], imm => stack-built: collect imms with capstone or\n266\t  emulate the builder with unicorn; (4) PE .rsrc / .NET resource / jar non-class entry / gaps between sections (slack) /\n267\t  custom ELF notes (`readelf -nW`) / compressed `C`-flag sections (`readelf -zx`) / archive appended after the image;\n268\t  (5) .init_array / TLS callback decoder => emulate it. Offsets: raw=the H, base64=the S (GM-confirmed); else first stored byte.\n269\tFIELDS: format = container only (elf/pe/macho?/jar; .NET pe_cli) | machine/architecture = container machine word |\n270\t  qualifier ids dNN_analysis_<tag>_<field> -> member whose file name has <tag> (stripped/symbolized, compact/direct, loader/\n271\t  plugin, D24 vulnerable/corrected; LONGEST member-name token); THEN the member the QUESTION names; \"decode both role members,\n272\t  require equal\" (D24) => decode all, assert equal, answer the common value ; sha256_K = zip archive order | config_* verbatim from HCFG JSON |\n273\t  has_<x>_section = literal section name | hex fields lowercase 0x | never chase the prompt's theme: answer only asked ids.\n274\t  New-language member = carried-over header ids (post first); twist = the NEW field family: its longest question is the\n275\t  spec (rules, offsets, transforms, hashes). `none` only for ABSENT things.\n276\tTHEME FACTS (unasked so far, backfill candidates): every member D2+ embeds a huntress.binary.dynamic_trace.v1 JSON template\n277\t  (branch, event_count, family \"<lang>_<theme>_trace\", effects, network) gated on env HUNTRESS_HOST_MODEL. D18 call graph;\n278\t  D21 NEEDED/exports/dlopen'd plugin header; D22 P/Invoke ImplMap; D23 predicates (Debugger.IsAttached, Stopwatch, CPU count,\n279\t  HUNTRESS_HOST_MODEL -> success/decoy/failure); D24 PATCH DIFF: `javap -p -c -constants` both twins' `$` classes + diff -> only\n280\t  `score(String)I` changed (null -> NPE fixed by Option guard, CWE-476). NEVER run such samples; ids were header + HCFG only.\n281\tBACKFILL ids on OLD groups (D8, D17): an unknown field on dNN = that day's own facts. Seen: marker (.huntress string),\n282\t  recover_code (decimal imm), mangled_score_symbol/typeinfo_symbol (bare _ZNK.../_ZTI...; PE .text$/.rdata$), has_go_runtime,\n283\t  has_rust_mangled_symbol, has_coroutine_runtime (enum true/false), methods (Main-Class method_info names incl <init>, JSON),\n284\t  access_flags (decimal, 49), method_count (incl <init>/<clinit>). Derive from bytes, POST all derivable ones together.\n285\thcfg_storage (enum): base64 carrier -> base64 | literal HCFG in section `.hcfg` -> raw_hcfg_section | in WASM data seg ->\n286\t  wasm_data_segment | in another native data section (.data/.rodata) -> raw_const_array | else raw. Stripped d01 => recover_code none.\n287\tUNGUESSABLE label: ~10 single-id probes max, HELP.md, then re-pull the contract (organizers revise it: enum + rule text).\n288\tFORWARD HINTS: grep each new contract for tokens/days not today's (open: enum `neko_bytecode`, \"for Day 26 use the primary\n289\t  classfile named by that unit\"). D22 renamed basenames, D23 TT/M re-shaped values (BRNN-<8hex>): key on `dNN--`, copy verbatim.\n290\t```\n291\t\n292\t## Readiness gaps\n293\t```json\n294\t[\n295\t  {\"id\": \"jvm-method-patch-diff-facts\", \"concept\": \"Backfill of the D24 theme on the d24 twin jars (and any future JVM twin): per-class/per-method bytecode diff of vulnerable vs corrected -- changed method name + descriptor, what changed, before/after facts\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Fixtures: the cached D24 jars (challenges/day24/binary-spot-the-difference/single_solve/work/extracted/evidence/d24--sample-{vulnerable,corrected}.jar; only `score(Ljava/lang/String;)I` in `Day24<Role>000$` differs). lib.binary.jvm_patch_diff(jar_a, jar_b) -> match classes after stripping the role token from class names (Day24Vulnerable000$ ~ Day24Corrected000$), match methods by name+descriptor, compare Code attributes with constant-pool operands RESOLVED to symbolic names (raw CP indexes shift between builds), ignore LineNumberTable/StackMapTable. Expose: changed_methods (JSON list of `name(descriptor)` or `name`), changed_class, unchanged_methods, method_count per member, code_length/instruction_count before/after, added/removed invoke targets (e.g. +scala/Option$.apply, +scala/Option.filter/map/getOrElse, -scala/collection/StringOps$.nonEmpty$extension), added invokedynamic lambdas (`$anonfun$score$N`), classfile sizes, fix_kind token (null_guard/bounds_check/length_check/exception_handler/constant_change). Labels unknown: prefer javap spellings (`score`, `(Ljava/lang/String;)I`) and read the question's rule text.\"},\n296\t  {\"id\": \"vulnerability-trigger-proof\", \"concept\": \"'Prove the old one was really broken': derive the triggering input for the changed function and each build's outcome statically (exception/fault vs safe return)\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"JVM: a tiny bytecode evaluator for leaf methods (aload/iconst/ifeq/ifnull/invoke of a stub model: java.lang.String length/charAt/isEmpty/equals/hashCode, scala Predef.augmentString (identity), StringOps.nonEmpty$extension/isEmpty, Option.apply/filter/map/getOrElse, BoxesRunTime) evaluated over a candidate set derived from the diff's guards (null, \\\"\\\", single char, index==length, -1, Integer.MIN/MAX); first input where the builds differ = trigger. Outcomes: `java.lang.NullPointerException` / `ArrayIndexOutOfBoundsException` / `StringIndexOutOfBoundsException` vs the corrected return (D24: null -> NPE vs -1). Native: unicorn-emulate the function with the trigger argument (map a stack, stub libc), report fault type/address. Never execute the sample itself. Facts: trigger_input, vulnerable_outcome, corrected_result, exception_class.\"},\n297\t  {\"id\": \"native-function-patch-diff\", \"concept\": \"Patch diff for native twin pairs (ELF/PE, C/C++/Rust/Go): which function changed and how (inserted bounds check, replaced unsafe call, changed constant/comparison)\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Likeliest sequel to D24 (the lane alternates languages; a C/C++ twin is the classic patch-diff). lib.binary.native_patch_diff(a, b): match functions by symbol, else by (call targets, referenced strings/imports, size, CFG shape); normalise capstone instructions (mask RIP-relative/absolute addresses and call targets, keep immediates) and hash per function; emit changed_functions (symbol names in address order), per-function added/removed instructions, inserted `cmp`+`ja/jae/jb/jbe` pairs (bounds check), replaced imports (strcpy->strncpy, gets->fgets, sprintf->snprintf, memcpy length change), changed frame size (`sub rsp, N`), comparison flips (`jl`->`jb` signedness, `jle`->`jl` off-by-one), added `test reg,reg; je` (null check). Fixtures: gcc -O0/-O2 vuln/fixed pairs for off-by-one, missing bounds check, strcpy overflow, signedness, format string, null-after-free; one stripped pair. Tools present: capstone, rz-diff (`rz-diff -t functions a b`), objdump.\"},\n298\t  {\"id\": \"vulnerability-class-classifier\", \"concept\": \"Name the bug class a fix addresses as a CWE token + snake_case name (null deref 476, OOB read 125 / write 787, off-by-one 193, int overflow 190, signedness 195, format string 134, UAF 416, double free 415, div-by-zero 369, unchecked return 252, TOCTOU 367, command injection 78, SQLi 89, path traversal 22, unsafe deserialization 502)\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Rule table over the diff facts of jvm-method-patch-diff-facts / native-function-patch-diff / managed-patch-diff-dotnet: added null guard / Option wrap / ifnull / `test;je` -> CWE-476; added index/length compare before array/charAt/memcpy -> 125/787; `<=`->`<` -> 193; `add`->`add.ovf`/Math.addExact/`__builtin_add_overflow` -> 190; `jl`->`jb` -> 195; printf(user)->printf(\\\"%s\\\",user) -> 134; free+null or use-after-free removal -> 416; divisor check -> 369; Runtime.exec/system/ProcessBuilder argument sanitising -> 78; ObjectInputStream.readObject filter -> 502; path normalise/`..` check -> 22. D24 fixture = CWE-476. Emit `CWE-476` and `null_pointer_dereference`; GM spelling unknown -> watch for an enum with accepted_values and read the question rules.\"},\n299\t  {\"id\": \"scala-module-class-facts\", \"concept\": \"Scala (and other JVM-language) identity facts for the d24 group backfill and the D26 'primary classfile named by that unit' rule: forwarder vs `$` module class, ScalaSignature/ScalaSig, TASTy, lambdas\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"D24 jars: `Day24<Role>000.class` = static forwarder (Main-Class, 1.2 KB) + `Day24<Role>000$.class` = module (MODULE$, encodedConfig, decodeConfig, score, main). Expose per member: main_class, primary_class (the class holding the logic / HCFG ldc = the `$` module), forwarder_class, has_scala_signature (RuntimeVisibleAnnotations `Lscala/reflect/ScalaSignature;` or `ScalaSig` attribute), scala_major (2 vs 3: `.tasty` entries / `TASTY` attribute), source_file (`Day24Vulnerable000.scala`), method lists + method_count of BOTH classes (incl <init>/<clinit>, table order), access_flags decimal, classfile major/minor, invokedynamic bootstrap count, `$anonfun$` synthetic methods. Also route 'primary classfile named by that unit' when the question names a class (take it verbatim) or a source unit (`X.scala` -> the class whose SourceFile matches and holds main/logic). Clojure (`<ns>__init.class`) / Groovy (`$getStaticMetaClass`) shapes as synthetic fixtures.\"},\n300\t  {\"id\": \"dotnet-il-callsite-facts\", \"concept\": \"IL body decoder for 'trace every crossing': per method the call/callvirt/calli/newobj targets (MethodDef/MemberRef/MethodSpec tokens -> Type::Name), ldstr user strings, ldsfld/ldtoken + RuntimeHelpers.InitializeArray (array blobs incl. F# `T<n>_<len>Bytes@` .text data), and which managed methods call each P/Invoke\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Parse method headers (tiny 0x2 / fat 0x3, 12-byte header, extra sections) at RVA, decode the full opcode table (single + 0xFE two-byte), resolve tokens through dnfile tables. Output: call graph edges managed->managed and managed->native (callers of each ImplMap method), user-string list in #US order, array-init blob offsets (maps the D22 HCFG @.text to the field that owns it). Fixtures: same C#/F# projects as dotnet-pinvoke-bridge-facts; verify against `ilspycmd -il`.\"},\n301\t  {\"id\": \"jni-java-native-bridge-pair\", \"concept\": \"JVM <-> native FFI pair: jar/class with ACC_NATIVE (0x0100) methods + System.loadLibrary(\\\"x\\\") + a `.so`/`.dll` exporting `Java_<pkg>_<Class>_<method>` (JNI name mangling `_1`=_, `_2`=;, `_3`=[, `_0xxxx`=unicode, `__` overload signature) or JNI_OnLoad + RegisterNatives JNINativeMethod {name, signature, fnPtr} tables\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"lib.binary.jni_bridge_facts(jar_bytes, so_bytes): native methods (class, name, descriptor) from the classfile, loadLibrary argument from the constant pool, exports demangled back to class/method, RegisterNatives triples by scanning .data.rel.ro for (char* name, char* sig, fnptr) with RELATIVE relocs, map each native method -> exported symbol/fn address; HCFG may sit in either member. Fixtures: javac + gcc -shared -I$JAVA_HOME/include (both installed); one static-export lib and one RegisterNatives lib; Kotlin `external fun` variant if kotlinc present.\"},\n302\t  {\"id\": \"member-basename-vocabulary\", \"concept\": \"Member basenames re-labelled between days (D22: `dNN--variant-000.*` -> `dNN--sample.*`, `sample-stripped`, `sample-plugin`) and questions reworded to match; D23 timed modes re-shaped the VALUES too (campaign `BRNN-<8 uppercase hex>`, d01 marker `BR01-<8hex>`, FILE symbol `sample.c`)\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"note\", \"detail\": \"Group members by the `dNN--` prefix only; derive role/tag from the token after the stem (stripped/symbolized, compact/direct, loader/plugin) or from the extension; never require `variant-` or `sample`. A regression case with renamed members (sed the names in a copy of the zip listing) keeps the router honest. D23: never regex-validate a value shape (`BRNN-\\\\d{3}`) or derive anything from the `00V` index; copy decoded values verbatim. D24 timed modes re-shaped domain (`<word>-<8hex>.dayNN.example.invalid`), mutex (`Global\\\\Huntress<12 uppercase hex>`) and url (`https://<word>-<8hex>.dayNN.example.invalid/<word>/<10hex>`) too; role tokens `vulnerable`/`corrected` follow `sample-`.\"},\n303\t  {\"id\": \"question-layout-parser-mutations\", \"concept\": \"Turn the question's layout prose into a struct and expose EVERY named field (any `<name>_size/_length/_offset/_sha256/_version/_count` id), robust to TT/Mastery mutations of the header\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"D20 needed a hand-written branch for the one unknown id (`hcfg_resource_size` = 'HCFG resource length u32le at +8'). Build lib.binary.layout_from_question(text) -> [(name, offset, type)] parsing phrases seen D19-D20: 'Read k1 at +5', 'X length u32le at +8', 'scratch length u16le at +12', 'bytes +16..+47 are the scratch SHA-256', 'the HCFG resource starts at +48, and scratch follows it', 'Verify exact end bounds'; also u8/u16be/u32be/u64le, 'relative to the overlay/file', 'immediately after'. Return a facts dict (fields + derived starts/ends + bound/hash checks) the solver can answer any matching id from by fuzzy name (resource_size == resource length). Fixtures: synthetic overlays with permuted fields, BE ints, renamed magic, extra padding, each with its question text; test that every id resolves.\"},\n304\t  {\"id\": \"contract-revision-watch\", \"concept\": \"Organizers revise the live contract mid-day (D17: exact_text -> enum + rule text)\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"note\", \"detail\": \"When an exact_text label resists ~10 probes: write HELP, then re-pull the contract (`hctf status <id>`) every ~20-30 min and diff question text/answer_format per id; D17 the revision converted ~3.5 h and ~10.9k rejected probes into CORRECT within a minute. Never run mass automated label grouptests on a closed-vocabulary GM field.\"},\n305\t  {\"id\": \"contract-forward-hints\", \"concept\": \"The live contract leaks upcoming days: tokens and day numbers that do not belong to today\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"note\", \"detail\": \"D19 leaked D20's overlay magic ('PK19 for Day 19 or RS20 for Day 20') and it came true. Still open after D21 (D20/D21 contracts added no new token; carried-over questions byte-identical): the format enum lists `neko_bytecode` (unseen), and d07_analysis_method_count says 'for Day 26 use the primary classfile named by that unit'. Each day, grep the contract for magic-like tokens (`[A-Z]{2}\\\\d{2}`), enum values never confirmed, and 'Day NN' > today; record them in solver/NOTES.md and the coverage atlas so the prebuild targets them. The solver maps a `<2 caps><NN>` magic to the group whose day is NN. D22: no new token/day; all members silently renamed dNN--variant-000.* -> dNN--sample.* and the d03 questions dropped 'variant-' -- solvers must not key on 'variant-'. D23: no new token/day either (Day 26 and neko_bytecode still open). D24: no new token/day; EVERY question reworded into a spec (sha256 'ZIP central-directory order (1-based)', format rule list, full HCFG layout + per-container carrier rule) -- Day 26 + neko_bytecode still open; D24 Scala's `Foo$` module vs forwarder Main-Class is a plausible meaning of 'primary classfile named by that unit'.\"},\n306\t  {\"id\": \"neko-bytecode-member\", \"concept\": \"Neko VM bytecode member (`.n`, magic NEKO): container parse, globals/strings, HCFG location, labels for format/architecture/machine\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"The GM's own format enum (d12-d19 since D19) lists `neko_bytecode` = a Neko member is scheduled. `apt install neko haxe` (candidates neko 2.4.1, haxe 4.3.7) then build fixtures: a Haxe `-neko out.n` program and a raw `nekoc` program holding the HCFG as a string literal (raw bytes and base64 'SENGR...') -- plus `nekotools boot` (Neko standalone ELF = neko VM + appended bytecode, another overlay!). Parser: 'NEKO' u32 nglobals, u32 nfields, u32 codesize; globals (type byte: 1 var, 2 function, 3 string u16/u32 len, 4 float, 5 debug, 6 version), fields (NUL-terminated names), code. Facts: format `neko_bytecode`, globals_count, fields list, string globals, hcfg offset (start of the string payload = the `H`/`S`), has_neko_runtime; architecture/machine for a VM are UNKNOWN -- record candidates (`neko`, `nekovm`, `none`) and read the question text first. Ensure lib.binary magic dispatch and the solver's format() return `neko_bytecode` for raw .n and recognise a nekotools-booted ELF (format elf + overlay).\"},\n307\t  {\"id\": \"theme-facts-recording\", \"concept\": \"Record each day's prompt-theme facts during the single solve (asked on its own day since D19, or in a later backfill)\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"note\", \"detail\": \"D5-D18 themes were never asked on their own day, but D19's (overlay_offset/overlay_size, config after unpacking) and D20's (overlay_offset, hcfg_resource_size) WERE and D17 backfilled D1-D7 single-solve facts on their old groups. After CORRECT, spend <=2 min writing the theme facts (stub/overlay header fields, call graph, branch map, imports, trace family/effects, decoder) into solver/NOTES.md under `THEME FACTS dNN:`; the solver's facts dict should already expose them as candidate field names (d19: overlay_version, k1/k2 hex, packed_length, unpacked_size, unpacked_sha256). d20: rs20 version, hcfg_resource_size, scratch_size (35), scratch_sha256, scratch text, image_end, GHC version 9.12.2. d21: loader/plugin NEEDED, plugin exports (caml_plugin_header, caml_globals, camlPlugin_000__entry), Caml2007D002 dynheader unit name Plugin_000, loader dlopen/caml_natdynlink_open imports, trace family ocaml_controlled_dynlink_trace / controlled_library_resolution_only, OCaml 4.02.3. d22: ModuleRef names (libc, kernel32.dll), ImplMap rows (import name, module, MappingFlags Winapi/charset not spec), calling MethodDefs, AssemblyRefs (System.Runtime, FSharp.Core, System.Text.Json, netstandard), FSharp resources, trace family fsharp_managed_native_bridge_trace / effects inert_native_process_id_bridge, HCFG .text @15891 + PE-overlay copy @18432. d23: VB.NET (Microsoft.VisualBasic.Core, StandardModuleAttribute, VB$AnonymousType_0`8), predicates Debugger.get_IsAttached / Stopwatch.StartNew+get_ElapsedTicks / Environment.get_ProcessorCount / GetEnvironmentVariable(HUNTRESS_HOST_MODEL) vs workstation/analysis/sandbox, branches success/decoy/failure, analysis_detected, trace vbnet_anti_analysis_predicate_trace / inert_predicate_only, HCFG PE overlay @7680 only. d24: changed method `score(Ljava/lang/String;)I` only (class `Day24<Role>000$`), vulnerable nonEmpty-then-charAt(0) (null -> NullPointerException, CWE-476) vs corrected Option(s).filter(nonEmpty).map(charAt 0).getOrElse(-1), $-class sizes 4660 vs 5628, main identical (host-model lookupswitch decoy 32 / success 49 / failure 27 / default failure 1, then score(\\\"benign\\\") + decodeConfig().length), trace scala_patch_diff_trace / benign_control_and_reversion_only + control_positive.\"},\n308\t  {\"id\": \"dotnet-anti-analysis-predicate-facts\", \"concept\": \"Backfill of the D23 theme on the d23 group: per anti-analysis predicate the API (Debugger.IsAttached/IsLogging, Stopwatch/DateTime.Now/Environment.TickCount64 timing, Environment.ProcessorCount/MachineName/UserName, GetEnvironmentVariable name), the compared constant (tick/ms threshold, CPU-count bound, env literal), the branch taken per HUNTRESS_HOST_MODEL value, and the analysis_detected verdict\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"D23 sample.dll (cached under challenges/day23/binary-trust-issues/single_solve/work/extracted/evidence/d23--sample.dll) is the fixture. Build on the prebuilt IL call-site decoder: walk Main's IL, record each call to a predicate API (MemberRef Type::Name), the following ldc.i4/ldc.i8/ldstr operand and the compare/branch opcode (bgt/blt/ceq/brtrue, VB Operators::CompareString), and the ldstr branch word each path stores (success/decoy/failure). Expose facts: predicate_count, predicates (JSON list in IL order, e.g. debugger_attached, timing, processor_count, env_host_model), env_var (HUNTRESS_HOST_MODEL), host_models (workstation/analysis/sandbox), branch_<model>, timing_threshold_ticks, cpu_threshold, trace_family, trace_effects. Labels unknown: prefer the API member name verbatim, decimal integers, enum tokens from the question. Never execute the sample.\"},\n309\t  {\"id\": \"static-predicate-branch-evaluator\", \"concept\": \"Evaluate env/host-model gated branches statically for ANY member (native or managed): given the predicate table, compute branch, event_count and analysis_detected for each host model without running the binary\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"'Spot every predicate and force the truth out' = the GM can ask 'which branch does host model X take' or 'the event_count on the analysis branch'. Native: capstone over main -- getenv(\\\"HUNTRESS_HOST_MODEL\\\") then strcmp/memcmp against rodata literals, cmp/jcc to blocks that load the branch string + event_count imm. Managed: IL from the predicate-facts builder. Fall back to angr (installed) with getenv hooked to each literal, ptrace/IsDebuggerPresent hooked to 0, clock calls hooked to constant deltas; never a real run. Fixtures: gcc C ELF with 3 env branches + debugger/timing checks, and the D23 dll.\"},\n310\t  {\"id\": \"anti-disassembly-tricks\", \"concept\": \"Anti-disassembly constructs that break linear sweep: overlapping instructions, jump into the middle of an instruction (`eb ff`), jz+jnz to the same target with junk after, `call $+5; pop`, fake `ret`/`push; ret` jumps, junk bytes in .text\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Evasion arc sequel to D23 ('doesn't trust you' -> 'don't trust your disassembler'). A `disassembly`/`recover_code`-style field on a function protected this way breaks objdump linear sweep. Build a recursive-descent capstone walker (follow both jcc edges, treat opposite-condition pairs as unconditional, stop at ret/jmp) that returns the real instruction list and the leaf constant; facts has_anti_disassembly + technique list. Fixtures: gcc -c with inline asm `.byte` junk, the jz/jnz trick and an overlapping `eb ff c0` sequence; compare against rizin `pdf`.\"},\n311\t  {\"id\": \"managed-string-decryptor-emulation\", \"concept\": \"Managed string encryption: a static decryptor method (ConfuserEx-style `<Module>` method, xor'd char/byte arrays, Base64+XOR, VB Chr/ChrW arithmetic) called in place of ldstr; JVM equivalents (static String a(int), invokedynamic StringConcatFactory, ZKM-style xor tables)\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"If the next day hides the HCFG or the predicate literals behind a managed decryptor, raw HCFG scans miss. Build: detect a method (int)->string or (byte[])->string called repeatedly, decode its IL into a tiny Python evaluator for the common ops (ldelem/xor/add/conv.u1/newobj String(char[]) / Encoding.UTF8.GetString / Convert.FromBase64String), apply it to every call site's operands, then hcfg_scan the results. JVM: same over javap -c bytecode. Fixtures: tiny C# and VB.NET programs compiled with `dotnet build` (dotnet installed) using an xor string helper; a javac class with a static xor decoder.\"},\n312\t  {\"id\": \"managed-patch-diff-dotnet\", \"concept\": \".NET twin assemblies (vulnerable/corrected dll): IL method-body diff by type+method+signature with token resolution\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Same contract as jvm-method-patch-diff-facts for pe_cli twins: dnfile MethodDef RVA -> IL bytes, decode with the prebuilt IL call-site decoder, resolve tokens to `Type::Method` / string literals, ignore metadata-token renumbering and MVID/timestamp; report changed_methods (`Namespace.Type::Method`), added `ldnull/brfalse`/`?.` null guards, `ldlen` bounds compares, `add.ovf` checked arithmetic, try/catch regions (exception clauses diff). Fixtures: D22/D23 cached dlls as single-build controls; build twins only if `dotnet build` works offline, else hand-patch IL bytes of a copy (same length) for a synthetic pair.\"},\n313\t  {\"id\": \"stripped-twin-function-matching\", \"concept\": \"Match functions between two STRIPPED native builds to find the patched one (no symbols): BinDiff/Diaphora-style heuristics\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"D15 shipped a stripped/symbolized pair; a stripped vulnerable/corrected pair is a natural escalation. Recover function starts (prologues, call targets, .eh_frame FDEs -- pyelftools CFI gives exact ranges even when stripped), then match by: referenced strings/imports, callee/caller sets, size, BB count, normalised-instruction hash, constant set; unmatched or hash-different = changed. Report the changed function's file offset/VA, its .eh_frame range and, if the symbolized twin exists in another group/member, its name. Fixtures: gcc pairs `strip -s`, -O2.\"},\n314\t  {\"id\": \"crash-exploitability-facts\", \"concept\": \"Native 'prove it is broken' facts: stack buffer size, distance from buffer to saved RIP/canary, overflow length that faults, faulting instruction, mitigations (canary/NX/PIE/RELRO)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"From capstone over the vulnerable function: frame size (`sub rsp, N`), buffer offset (`lea rdi, [rbp-0xNN]` passed to gets/strcpy/read/memcpy/scanf %s), canary load `mov rax, fs:0x28` + `__stack_chk_fail`, read length argument; distance_to_return = NN + 8 (rbp) ; first faulting length via unicorn emulation with a cyclic (de Bruijn) pattern; checksec-style facts from program headers (GNU_STACK flags, GNU_RELRO + BIND_NOW, ET_DYN+INTERP). Corrected twin: same facts showing the bound. Fixtures: gcc -fno-stack-protector / -fstack-protector-strong pairs.\"},\n315\t  {\"id\": \"binary-patch-file-apply\", \"concept\": \"Binary patch FILES as group members applied to a base member: bsdiff (`BSDIFF40`, bz2 blocks), IPS (`PATCH` ... `EOF`), BPS/UPS (`BPS1`/`UPS1` + crc32), xdelta3/VCDIFF (`d6 c3 c4 00`), unified diff text\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"'Two builds, one fix' could next ship base + patch instead of two builds. Pure-Python appliers (no bsdiff4/xdelta3 binaries assumed): bsdiff40 (header 32 B: ctrl/diff lengths + new size, three bz2 streams), IPS records (u24 offset, u16 size, RLE when size 0), BPS (varint actions + source/target/patch crc32), VCDIFF RFC 3284 (no secondary compressor). Facts: patch_format, target_size, target_sha256, changed byte ranges / count, patched function (map offsets through the section table), crc checks valid. Fixtures: generate with Python writers for each format over a small ELF.\"},\n316\t  {\"id\": \"symbolic-input-solver\", \"concept\": \"Find an input that reaches a target (vulnerable path, accept branch, decoy vs success) with angr/z3 when hand-evaluation is impractical: crackme/license checks, multi-step guards\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"angr (venv) blank_state at the function with symbolic args/stdin, avoid-list = failure branches, find = target address (crash site, success string xref, `return 1`); z3 directly for JVM/IL guard chains extracted by the bytecode evaluators (hashCode lookupswitch -> string preimage among the binary's own literals first). Hard caps: 60 s, 4 GB; output the concrete input as hex + printable. Fixtures: gcc serial-check (per-char xor/add compare), a hash-gated branch, and the D24 host-model lookupswitch (preimages analysis/workstation/sandbox).\"},\n317\t  {\"id\": \"dotnet-pinvoke-bridge-facts\", \"concept\": \".NET P/Invoke bridge facts as answer fields (the unasked D22 theme): per P/Invoke method the managed name, ImportName (entry point), ModuleRef name as written (`libc`, `kernel32.dll`), calling convention token, charset, SetLastError/ExactSpelling/BestFit flags, marshaled param/return types from the MethodDef signature blob + FieldMarshal, counts and table order; also LibraryImport-generated stubs, `delegate* unmanaged`, UnmanagedCallersOnly (reverse P/Invoke), NativeLibrary.Load/GetExport + Marshal.GetDelegateForFunctionPointer string targets\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"lib.binary.dotnet_pinvoke_facts(data) via dnfile: rows of md.ImplMap joined to md.ModuleRef and the MethodDef (Flags PinvokeImpl 0x2000, RVA 0); decode ECMA-335 MethodDefSig (ELEMENT_TYPE_* -> C# keyword and raw name), MappingFlags -> tokens (winapi/cdecl/stdcall/thiscall/fastcall; ansi/unicode/auto/none). Fixtures: `dotnet new console` C# + `dotnet new console -lang F#` projects with [DllImport(\\\"libc\\\")] getpid, [DllImport(\\\"kernel32.dll\\\", SetLastError=true, CharSet=Unicode)], [LibraryImport] partial method, a function-pointer call; check against ilspycmd output. Expose as candidate fields: pinvoke_count, pinvoke_imports (JSON), native_modules (JSON, ModuleRef order), <method>_module.\"},\n318\t  {\"id\": \"native-imports-exports-facts\", \"concept\": \"imports / NEEDED / interpreter / exports lists for ELF, PE, Mach-O\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"BUILT (prebuild-state ok). Generic facts: ELF `needed` (DT_NEEDED order), `imports` (UND .dynsym names, table order, version suffix stripped), `interpreter` (.interp without NUL), `exports` (defined dynsyms); PE import dll list + functions ... D21 THEME (unasked on D21): loader NEEDED libm/libdl/libc, plugin NEEDED libc + weak __cxa_finalize/__gmon_start__/_ITM_*; expose these for a d21 backfill.\"},\n319\t  {\"id\": \"multi-role-member-router\", \"concept\": \"Groups of 3+ members with roles (loader + several plugins/libraries, stub + payload, client + server), HCFG in one member only, decoy HCFG in another; ids qualified by role or unqualified with the member named in the question text\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"D21 needed a hand-written _named_member() for unqualified ids whose question says 'Use the d21-- plugin.cmxs member; the loader has no scored HCFG config' and it had to run AFTER the qualifier peel. Generalize into lib.binary.route_member(group, field, question) -> (member, residual_field): qualifier peel by longest file-name token, then question phrases ('basename ends X', 'Use the dNN-- X member', 'the member that exports Y', 'the library named by the loader's DT_NEEDED', 'the member loaded by ...'), then structural fallbacks (the only member with a crc-valid HCFG for config_*). Regression: D15/D16/D21 shapes + synthetic 3-member groups (loader, plugin_a, plugin_b) with a decoy HCFG (bad crc) in the loader. D22 SEEN as primary + support members (sample.dll + runtimeconfig.json + FSharp.Core.dll), no id qualifier; the question names the primary ('unique d22-- primary managed assembly ... dependency DLL members are delivery support only').\"},\n320\t  {\"id\": \"ffi-boundary-exports\", \"concept\": \"Cross-language ABI boundaries: C-ABI exports from Rust cdylib (#[no_mangle]), Go c-shared (cgo `_cgo_`, `crosscall2`, `_cgoexp_`), JNI (`Java_<pkg>_<cls>_<m>`, JNI_OnLoad), Python extension (`PyInit_<mod>`), OCaml C stubs (`caml_*` CAMLprim)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"'mind the boundaries' + one-language-per-day: the next pair may be a non-C plugin. lib.binary.ffi_facts(data): ffi kind token (rust_cdylib/go_c_shared/jni/python_ext/ocaml_stub/plain_c), exported C names in dynsym order, demangled JNI class/method from the export name, Go c-shared buildinfo. Fixtures: gcc .so with JNI-shaped exports + a PyInit_ export; use cargo/go c-shared builds only if those toolchains are present, else synthetic dynsym names. D22 ('P/Invoke and FFI') shipped only the .NET side (ImplMap getpid@libc, GetCurrentProcessId@kernel32.dll); the native side of an FFI pair (JNI .so, ctypes/extension .so, N-API .node) is the likeliest follow-up -- see jni-java-native-bridge-pair / native-extension-bridges.\"},\n321\t  {\"id\": \"dynlink-handshake-facts\", \"concept\": \"Loader/plugin handshake facts for a dlopen-style pair (the unasked D21 theme): which member loads which, the dlopen'd path string, dlsym'd symbol names, the plugin's init/registration export and header struct\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"D21 = OCaml loader ELF (imports caml_natdynlink_open/caml_dlopen, NEEDED libdl, string 'not an OCaml plugin') + .cmxs plugin exporting caml_plugin_header -> marshalled dynheader with magic `Caml2007D002`, unit list (name `Plugin_000`, crc, defines/imports). Build lib.binary.dynlink_facts(loader, plugin) for (a) OCaml natdynlink (parse caml_plugin_header VA -> file offset, magic, unit names), (b) C dlopen/dlsym (string args near the call: resolve `lea rdi,[rip+x]` before `call dlopen@plt`/`dlsym@plt` with capstone; plugin `plugin_init`/`*_register` exports), (c) PE LoadLibraryA/W + GetProcAddress (string args, DLL export by name/ordinal). Fields: plugin_header_magic, plugin_units (JSON), loaded_library, resolved_symbols (JSON, call order), init_export, plugin_exports (dynsym order, defined only). Fixtures: gcc loader+.so pair with a .hcfg in the .so; synthetic OCaml-shaped .so with a caml_plugin_header pointing at a `Caml2007D002` blob.\"},\n322\t  {\"id\": \"relocation-got-plt-facts\", \"concept\": \"Relocation tables as answers and as storage: .rela.dyn/.rela.plt counts per type (JUMP_SLOT, GLOB_DAT, RELATIVE, IRELATIVE, COPY), PLT slot -> import name, lazy vs BIND_NOW, RELRO, and HCFG pieces reachable only through RELATIVE addends\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Next 'linking' concept after D21 ('mind the boundaries'). lib.binary.elf_reloc_facts(data): per-section relocation list (offset, type name as readelf prints it e.g. R_X86_64_JUMP_SLOT, symbol, addend), counts, plt_imports (JSON in .rela.plt order), bind_now (DT_FLAGS BIND_NOW or DF_1_NOW), relro full/partial/none. Storage twist: a PIE whose HCFG chunks are pointed to by a pointer table filled only by R_X86_64_RELATIVE addends (bytes zero on disk) -> apply relocations to a copy of the image, then hcfg_scan the relocated image; also GOT entries pointing at config. Fixtures via gcc -fPIE -pie / -Wl,-z,now / -Wl,-z,lazy.\"},\n323\t  {\"id\": \"symbol-versioning-interposition\", \"concept\": \"GNU symbol versioning and interposition: .gnu.version/_d/_r, default vs hidden versions (foo@@V2 / foo@V1), binding (GLOBAL/WEAK/LOCAL/UNIQUE), visibility, and LD_PRELOAD-style shims that export libc names\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"lib.binary.elf_version_facts(data): verdefs (name, flags, index), verneeds (file -> [version names]) in table order, per-dynsym version string, weak symbols, interposed libc names (defined dynsyms whose name is a libc import name: open, getenv, dlsym, __libc_start_main) and whether they call dlsym(RTLD_NEXT). Labels as readelf -V / --dyn-syms prints (`GLIBC_2.2.5`, `@@`). Fixtures: gcc -shared with a version script (-Wl,--version-script) defining V1/V2 of a config getter whose V2 returns the HCFG and V1 a decoy; an LD_PRELOAD shim .so.\"},\n324\t  {\"id\": \"library-search-path-facts\", \"concept\": \"How the loader resolves libraries: DT_RPATH vs DT_RUNPATH (incl. $ORIGIN/$LIB tokens), PT_INTERP path, DT_FLAGS_1 (NOW, PIE, NODEFLIB, ORIGIN), SONAME, dlopen path argument absolute/relative\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"D21 trace effects = `controlled_library_resolution_only` -> resolution facts are a likely backfill/next-day field family. lib.binary.elf_loader_facts(data): interpreter, needed (order), soname, rpath, runpath (raw string, not expanded), flags/flags_1 token lists as readelf prints them, has_origin. Plus resolve_library(loader, name, members) that maps a NEEDED/dlopen name to the group member that satisfies it (SONAME match first, then basename). Fixtures: gcc -Wl,-rpath,'$ORIGIN/lib' vs --enable-new-dtags, -Wl,-soname, custom --dynamic-linker.\"},\n325\t  {\"id\": \"resource-table-overlay\", \"concept\": \"Multi-entry resource directory overlays: magic + count + N fixed-size entries (name/type id, offset, size, sha256/crc) + data, select the HCFG entry by name/type\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Natural escalation of D20's single-resource RS20 ('map every boundary'). Synthetic fixtures: ELF + appended table with 2-5 entries (HCFG, decoy HCFG with bad crc, scratch, icon), offsets relative to the overlay vs the file, names as fixed 8-byte/NUL-padded or length-prefixed strings. Fields to expose: resource_count, resource_names (JSON, table order), per-entry offset/size/sha256, selected entry index, boundaries [[start,end],...]. Reuse question-layout-parser output for the header.\"},\n326\t  {\"id\": \"section-slack-cave-storage\", \"concept\": \"Bytes past the end of the sections but INSIDE the image: inter-section padding, section tail slack inside its PT_LOAD segment, gap between program headers and the first section, gap before the section-header table\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"D20 prompt: 'bytes past the end of the sections ... map every boundary'. Build lib.binary.elf_file_map(data) -> ordered list of covered ranges (ELF header, PHDRs, each non-NOBITS section, SHT, overlay) and UNCOVERED gaps with (start, end, size, entropy, nonzero bytes, containing segment). Fixtures: gcc ELF with HCFG patched into the alignment gap before .text / after .rodata / before e_shoff, and one with the gap inside a PT_LOAD (code cave). Fields: cave_offset/size, gap list JSON, hcfg_storage for a gap (probably `raw` per the D17 rule list). Same for PE (between section raw ends and next PointerToRawData).\"},\n327\t  {\"id\": \"appended-archive-sfx\", \"concept\": \"Archive appended to an executable (zip/escript/SWI-Prolog saved state/zipapp, tar, 7z, squashfs AppImage, cpio): find it, fix relative offsets, read the HCFG member\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Cues: `PK\\\\x05\\\\x06` EOCD near EOF whose cd_offset is relative to the archive start (python zipfile tolerates prepended data; record archive_start = len - (eocd_off - cd_offset ... )), `hsqs` squashfs (AppImage runtime ELF + squashfs at the ELF image end), `7z\\\\xbc\\\\xaf\\\\x27\\\\x1c`, `ustar` at +257. Fixtures: ELF + zip(HCFG.json), ELF + tar, ELF + squashfs (mksquashfs if installed, else synthetic header only). Expose archive_offset, archive_format, member names (central-directory order), member sha256. AES zip inside? use the GM password `infected` only if the question says so.\"},\n328\t  {\"id\": \"question-spec-overlay-unpacker\", \"concept\": \"Generic overlay unpacker driven by the QUESTION TEXT: magic, header field offsets/widths, keys, packed length, hash, per-byte transform expression\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"D19 config questions said: 'Find the final PK19 overlay. Read k1 at +5, k2 at +6, packed length u32le at +8, the 32-byte unpacked SHA-256 at +12, and packed bytes at +44. For each packed byte compute ror8(byte XOR k2,3) XOR k1; verify the unpacked SHA-256 and use the HCFG record at unpacked offset 0.' D20 announces `RS20` with a likely different layout. Build lib.binary.overlay_spec(question) -> {magic, fields{name:(off, fmt u8/u16le/u32le/u32be/bytes[n])}, data_off, hash(sha256/crc32/md5, field), transform AST} and overlay_unpack(data, spec) -> (offset, size, header, out, hash_ok). Transform grammar: XOR/ADD/SUB (mod 256), ror8/rol8(x,n), NOT, nibble swap, index terms (i, i mod n, key[i % len]), previous-byte chaining (prev plain/cipher), reversed order, keystream words (RC4(key), LCG(seed,a,c)), followed by optional zlib/lzma/RLE decompress. Reject (return None) when the hash fails; never guess. Fixtures: the cached D19 member (single + the Mastery/TT deliveries if cached) and synthetic RS20-style overlays for each grammar item with their question sentences; the D19 solver's overlay_unpack/overlay_magic in challenges/day19/binary-jack-in-the-box/solver/solve.py is the reference.\"},\n329\t  {\"id\": \"overlay-header-facts\", \"concept\": \"Overlay/packer header facts as fields for the d19 group (and RS20): has_overlay, overlay_magic, overlay_version, k1_hex/k2_hex, packed_length, unpacked_size, unpacked_sha256, image_end\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"D19 asked only overlay_offset/overlay_size + config after unpacking; the D17 pattern means the header fields get asked within days (or on the d19 group in a backfill). From the PK19 header: magic `PK19`, version byte 4 (1), k1 byte 5 / k2 byte 6 as `0x%02x` (like xor_key_hex), pad byte 7, packed_length u32le +8 (380), unpacked_sha256 = 64 lowercase hex (+12..+44, no prefix, like artifact sha256), unpacked_size = len(out), packed_sha256, image_end (e_shoff + e_shnum*e_shentsize) and overlay == image_end boolean, overlay_entropy. Expose in the solver facts dict with plain names (overlay_version, k1_hex, k2_hex, packed_length, unpacked_length, unpacked_sha256, has_overlay=true/false) and a generic hcfg_storage answer for a packed blob (rule list: no section contains it -> `raw`? record as uncertain; read the enum text). Tests: cached D19 member + synthetic overlays.\"},\n330\t  {\"id\": \"fortran-gfortran-deep-facts\", \"concept\": \"gfortran facts for the d18 group when its theme is backfilled: source file name, MAIN__, internal procedures (name.N), select_string case table, libgfortran imports, .comment GCC banner\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"BUILT (prebuild-state ok). Fixtures: copy the cached d18 members (single variant-000 + TT/Mastery variants under challenges/day18/binary-flow-state/solver/cases/*/artifacts) into tests/data/binary_fixtures (gfortran compiler is NOT installed; runtime libgfortran.so.5 is). Facts: source_file `variant-000.f90` (STT_FILE), main_program `MAIN__`, procedures [event_failure, event_sandbox, event_decoy, event_success] with and without the `.N` suffix (table order + address order), case table = `_gfortran_select_string` struct array {low_ptr, low_len, high_ptr, high_len, case_no} x N (entry 0 = default, NULL ptrs) -> [(case_string, case_no)] e.g. analysis->1, sandbox->2, workstation->3, env var `HUNTRESS_HOST_MODEL` (the edi string passed to _gfortran_get_environment_variable_i4), imports list (9 `_gfortran_*`), NEEDED [libgfortran.so.5, libm.so.6, libgcc_s.so.1, libc.so.6], hcfg symbol `encoded_config.4`. Expose all as facts-dict keys with plain names (procedures, case_values, env_var, needed, imports, source_file).\"},\n331\t  {\"id\": \"callgraph-indirect-flow-facts\", \"concept\": \"Generic call graph with indirect-call resolution for ELF/PE: per-function callees, PLT import edges, `mov/lea reg, imm; call reg` targets, call-table/jump-table targets, entry->main chain\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"BUILT (prebuild-state ok). D18 prompt: 'Reconstruct the call graph ... follow the calls' (unasked). Implement lib.binary.call_graph(data) with capstone linear sweep over FUNC symbols (fallback: .eh_frame FDE ranges / rizin `aaa;aflj` when stripped): direct `call rel32` -> callee symbol or PLT import name (resolve via .rela.plt), `call reg` resolved by backward scan for `mov e/rax, imm32` or `lea rax, [rip+x]` in the same block, `call [rip+x]` via GOT/data pointer. Output edges [[caller, callee, kind(direct|plt|indirect)]] in address order, plus indirect_call_count, indirect_targets, functions_reached_from(main). Fixtures: d18 Fortran (4 indirect `call rax` to event_*), d01 C, d15 stripped/symbolized pair, a PE (d02 MinGW). Candidate GM shapes: JSON array of callee names, integer counts, `none` when stripped.\"},\n332\t  {\"id\": \"api-intent-injection-classifier\", \"concept\": \"Classify each imported/called API by intent and give an injection verdict (ELF + PE), mapping to MITRE T1055.x\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"BUILT (prebuild-state ok). D18 prompt: 'read the API intent at each edge, and prove no injection hides in the flow'; trace effects `modeled_process_access_no_injection`. Table (lib/knowledge.py-style dict, not lib edits by workers): env_query (getenv, _gfortran_get_environment_variable_i4, GetEnvironmentVariable), output (printf/puts/write/_gfortran_st_write*), string (strcmp/_gfortran_select_string/string_len_trim), process_access (ptrace ATTACH/PEEK, OpenProcess, /proc/<pid>/mem read), injection (ptrace POKETEXT/POKEDATA/SETREGS, process_vm_writev, VirtualAllocEx+WriteProcessMemory+CreateRemoteThread, NtMapViewOfSection, QueueUserAPC, SetWindowsHookEx, SetThreadContext, LD_PRELOAD/dlopen of a written file, memfd_create+execve), network (socket/connect/WSAStartup/WinHttp*). Facts: api_intents {name: intent}, has_injection (true/false), injection_apis [] , process_access_apis. Fixtures: d18 (no injection), plus small gcc/MinGW-free fixtures that import process_vm_writev / ptrace (PE: build import table with pefile or use existing PE fixtures).\"},\n333\t  {\"id\": \"dynamic-trace-template-facts\", \"concept\": \"Parse the `huntress.binary.dynamic_trace.v1` trace template embedded in every member (D2-D18) and model its env-gated branches\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"BUILT (prebuild-state ok). Every member carries a format template like `{\\\"schema\\\":\\\"huntress.binary.dynamic_trace.v1\\\",\\\"branch\\\":\\\"<b>\\\",\\\"event_count\\\":<n>,\\\"campaign\\\":\\\"BRNN-00V\\\",\\\"family\\\":\\\"fortran_indirect_flow_trace\\\",\\\"effects\\\":\\\"modeled_process_access_no_injection\\\",\\\"network\\\":\\\"none\\\"}` (jar: constant-pool strings; wasm: data segment; some keys filled at runtime: manifest_entries, archive_score, selector `eventCountForModel:` on ObjC). Families seen: d10 non_mutating_service_plan, d11 synthetic_document_manifest, d12 private_scratch_archive_manifest, d14 non_mutating_trigger_plan, d15 symbol_loss_equivalent_trace, d17 ada_encoded_config_trace, d18 fortran_indirect_flow_trace. Extract per member: schema, family, effects, network, static key list, host-model options (`analysis`/`sandbox`/`workstation`), env var name (`HUNTRESS_HOST_MODEL`), and the branch/event chosen per option (static from the case table / compare chain; optional sandboxed run under bwrap with --unshare-net and the env set, ELF x86-64 only, never on the host). Facts keys: trace_schema, trace_family, trace_effects, trace_network, host_model_env, host_models, branch_for_<model>.\"},\n334\t  {\"id\": \"hcfg-storage-classifier\", \"concept\": \"Generic `hcfg_storage` token for EVERY group/container per the D17 GM rule list (base64 / raw_hcfg_section / wasm_data_segment / raw_const_array / raw)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"BUILT (prebuild-state ok). D17 asked it on d08/d09/d11-d14 only; the next backfill likely spreads it (as hcfg_offset spread) to d02 (ELF `.hcfg` or PE `.hcfg` COFF section), d03 (.NET FieldRVA blob inside PE `.text` -> by the rules `raw_const_array` only if the section is a data section, else `raw` -- record both as uncertain), d04 Go/d05 Rust/d17 Ada `.rodata` (raw_const_array), d06/d07 jars (base64 in a deflated constant pool -> `base64`), d10 `.hcfg` (raw_hcfg_section), d15 pair, d16 wasm (wasm_data_segment). Implement `lib.binary.hcfg_storage(data, hit)` = rules applied in order over (hit.encoding, container, section containing hit.offset with its flags: SHF_ALLOC && !SHF_EXECINSTR = data; PE IMAGE_SCN_CNT_INITIALIZED_DATA; Mach-O __DATA/__DATA_CONST/__TEXT,__const). Tests: every cached day02-day17 member on disk (GM-confirmed d08/d09/d11-d14 tokens as expected values) + synthetic `.hcfg`/.data/.rodata/.text/PE/wasm fixtures; return None (not a guess) when the hit lies in no section.\"},\n335\t  {\"id\": \"question-rule-extractor\", \"concept\": \"Read the contract's per-id rule text + `accepted_values` and enforce it pre-submit (organizer revisions turn labels into enums)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"BUILT (prebuild-state ok). D17: the organizers re-issued the contract mid-day; hcfg_storage became kind enum with accepted_values and 'Apply these mutually exclusive rules in order: <token> when <cond>; ...; otherwise <token>'. Build a lane helper that (a) parses `(token, condition)` pairs out of such question text, (b) exposes `accepted_values` per id to the solver, (c) refuses to emit a token outside accepted_values (empty + log instead), (d) diffs two contract snapshots per id (question/answer_format changed) so a stuck worker sees the revision immediately. Tests: D17 single_solve morning vs revised contract.json (both on disk if cached; otherwise synthetic pair).\"},\n336\t  {\"id\": \"offset-section-mapper\", \"concept\": \"Map a file offset to its container location: ELF section + segment (name, flags, VA), PE section (name, RVA, VA), Mach-O segment,section, WASM data segment index + memory offset\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"BUILT (prebuild-state ok). Underpins hcfg_storage and the likely next location ids (`hcfg_section`, `hcfg_va`/`hcfg_vaddr`, `hcfg_rva`, `hcfg_segment`, `hcfg_mem_offset`). `lib.binary.locate_offset(data, off)` -> {container, section, section_flags, segment_index, vaddr, rva, wasm_data_index, wasm_mem_offset}; pure struct parsing (no pyelftools exceptions on sstripped files: fall back to program headers). Expected spellings to try first: section name verbatim (`.rodata`), VA as lowercase `0x` hex like entry_point. Tests on cached day08-day17 members (D17 Ada blob at file 207432 in `.rodata`, D14 at 4000 in `.hcfg`, D12 at 82928 in `.data`) and the wasm fixtures.\"},\n337\t  {\"id\": \"elf-header-segment-facts\", \"concept\": \"Remaining ELF header + program-header facts as fields: e_flags, os_abi, abi_version, e_phnum/e_shnum/e_shstrndx, segments list (p_type order), interpreter, GNU_STACK/RELRO/PIE/static booleans\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"NOT BUILT (1st attempt killed rc -9, nothing written: keep the scope small -- pyelftools only, no Ghidra). Backfills so far asked elf_class, elf_type, endianness, entry_point, section_names, symbols, has_symtab. Next cheap carry-over ids: `segments`/`program_headers` (JSON of p_type names readelf-style `LOAD`/`PT_LOAD`? both recorded), `segment_count`, `section_count` (incl. NULL), `interpreter` (`/lib64/ld-linux-x86-64.so.2`), `os_abi` (`UNIX - System V` vs `ELFOSABI_SYSV` vs 0), `is_pie`/`is_static`/`has_nx`/`relro` (`full`/`partial`/`none`), `e_flags` hex. Implement in the solver facts dict (lib.binary helper) with GM-style spellings mirroring the confirmed ones (ET_EXEC style for enums, lowercase 0x hex, decimal counts). Tests: cached day01-day17 ELF members + readelf parity.\"},\n338\t  {\"id\": \"ada-gnat-deep-facts\", \"concept\": \"Ada/GNAT facts for the d17 group when its own theme is backfilled: GNAT version, binder/elaboration symbols, Ada subprogram names, decoder function, exception ids\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"BUILT (prebuild-state ok). D17 prompt ('recover the reversible decoder') was unasked; the D17 backfill pattern means d17 facts get asked within days. From the cached Ada ELF (single_solve/work/extracted d17 member): gnat_version (`GNAT Version: 14.2.0` -> `14.2.0`), has_gnat_runtime (`__gnat_`/`ada__`/`system__`), main/binder symbols (`_ada_<main>`, `adainit`, `adafinal`, `__gnat_main`?), Ada-encoded names `pkg__sub` -> `pkg.sub` (keep mangled when asked for symbols), DWARF producer `GNU Ada 14.2.0` / DW_LANG_Ada95/2005, decoder routine name (function whose code xrefs the blob VA, via decoder-routine-locator) and its xor immediate (== header key?). Return none/false on absence; never raise.\"},\n339\t  {\"id\": \"qemu-user-static\", \"concept\": \"Run/observe foreign-arch ELF decoders (ARM/AArch64/MIPS/PPC/RISC-V)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"tool\", \"detail\": \"apt install qemu-user-static binfmt-support (only qemu-system-* are installed now). Use only inside the bwrap sandbox, never on the host; static analysis remains the default.\"},\n340\t  {\"id\": \"diec\", \"concept\": \"Compiler/packer/language fingerprint for unknown toolchains\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"tool\", \"detail\": \"github release horsicq/DIE-engine (die_lin64_portable tar) -> `diec -j F`. Complements `rz-bin -I` lang= and the STEP 3 strings regex when a new language lands.\"},\n341\t  {\"id\": \"checksec-fields\", \"concept\": \"PIE/RELRO/NX/canary/static as answer fields\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"note\", \"detail\": \"`rz-bin -I` already prints pic/relro/nx/canary/static/stripped. GM spelling unknown: relro full/partial/none, booleans true/false like has_symtab. Add to playbook naming law before first sighting; no checksec install needed.\"},\n342\t  {\"id\": \"new-language-fingerprints\", \"concept\": \"V, Odin, Modula-2, Kotlin/Native, Dart AOT, Nuitka, Erlang, Julia, Zig-cc/Nim-js... (Ada D17, Fortran D18, COBOL D19, Haskell D20, OCaml D21 seen)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"note\", \"detail\": \"Cue strings are in the Recognition cues STEP 3 regex. All still answer format=elf/architecture=x86-64 per the D8-D15 law; risk is only where the HCFG literal lives (compressed Dart snapshot, Nuitka constants blob, GHC closures) -> hcfg_scan then Ghidra. Ada/Fortran/COBOL/Haskell/OCaml all landed as plain x86-64 ELFs (format elf) -- the law held; D19-D20 moved the HCFG into an overlay, D21 into a separate plugin member. gfortran/gnat/ocaml/ghc are NOT installed for fixture builds (apt gfortran gnat ocaml-nox ghc if prebuilds are wanted).\"},\n343\t  {\"id\": \"kotlin-native-member\", \"concept\": \"Kotlin/Native ELF (konanc): `kfun:` symbols, Konan runtime, HCFG in an object literal\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Kotlin already appeared as a jar (D7); a native build is a plausible 'pair the language with a new container' twist. Cues: `kfun:` / `kclass:` / `ktype:` symbols, `Konan_main`, `Kotlin_` runtime, `kotlin.native.internal`. Strings are UTF-16 in KString objects -> hcfg_scan utf16 path + offset = first stored byte (speculative). Facts: has_kotlin_native_runtime, kfun names. Fixture: C ELF with those symbol names + UTF-16LE base64 blob.\"},\n344\t  {\"id\": \"pe-optional-header-facts\", \"concept\": \"PE/COFF facts for the PE members (d02 MinGW, d03 .NET, d10 Zig PE, d04 Go .exe): subsystem, image_base, timestamp, characteristics, dll_characteristics, section names (NUL-trimmed), entry RVA/VA, imports\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"PE members re-roll into Mastery for d02/d04/d10; a backfill on them would ask the ELF-equivalent fields: format pe, machine, entry_point (ImageBase+AddressOfEntryPoint as 0x hex?), section_names (PE names, `/4` long names resolved via COFF string table), subsystem (`console`/`IMAGE_SUBSYSTEM_WINDOWS_CUI`/3), image_base, has_symtab (COFF symbol table present), timestamp (decimal). pefile installed. Tests: cached MinGW/Zig/Go/.NET PE members from day02-day16 artifacts + record both spelling families.\"},\n345\t  {\"id\": \"jumptable-switch-recovery\", \"concept\": \"Recover switch/SELECT CASE dispatch: gcc relative int32 tables (`movsxd rax,[rdx+rax*4]; add rax,rdx; jmp rax`), absolute 8-byte tables, MSVC/MinGW tables, gfortran select_string case arrays, Go/Rust match tables\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"D18 dispatched on `_gfortran_select_string` + cmp chain; a stripped or -O2 sequel uses a real jump table. Implement lib.binary.switch_tables(data): find `jmp reg` preceded by a bounded index (cmp/ja) and a table base (lea rip+x), read N entries, map case -> target address -> symbol. Fixtures: clang-18/gcc -O2 C switch with 6+ dense cases (ELF + `-static`), the d18 case table, an AArch64 `br x` table (aarch64-linux-gnu-gcc). Output: [{case, target, symbol}] and case_count.\"},\n346\t  {\"id\": \"flattened-dispatcher-recovery\", \"concept\": \"Control-flow flattening (OLLVM-style state-variable dispatcher) and opaque predicates: recover the original block order / state transitions\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Title pun 'Flow State' -> state machine; OLLVM is not installed, so hand-write fixtures: C with `switch(state)` inside `while(1)` where each case sets the next state (constants xor'd), plus opaque predicates `x*(x+1)%2==0`. Extractor: identify the dispatcher (block with most predecessors + cmp/jmp on one stack var), emulate each case with unicorn to read the next-state constant, output the state sequence [s0, s1, ...], the executed block order, and the final return value (ties into emulate-return-value). Fixtures in ELF x86-64 and one MinGW-free PE via existing PE fixture style.\"},\n347\t  {\"id\": \"gcc-frontend-modula2-member\", \"concept\": \"Next GCC front-end languages as a new-day member: Modula-2 (gm2), COBOL (gcobol, GCC 15), Algol 68 (ga68), gccgo\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"NOT BUILT (1st attempt failed). D17 Ada, D18 Fortran, D19 GnuCOBOL: the organizers walk a 'legacy/GCC-family language' list, each landing as a plain dynamic ELF. Remaining: Modula-2 (gm2: NEEDED libm2pim/libm2iso/libm2rts, `_M2_<Module>_init`/`_fini`), gccgo (libgo.so.23, `__go_`, `.go_export`, NO `.go.buildinfo`), Algol 68 (ga68), gcobol (GCC 15 COBOL: `libgcobol.so`, `__gg__` -- differs from D19's libcob). Keep the scope small: add the cue strings to lib.binary.language_of + synthetic fixtures (C ELF with those NEEDED/symbol names and a raw `.rodata` HCFG); compilers only if `apt-cache policy gm2 gccgo` shows a candidate.\"},\n348\t  {\"id\": \"multi-layer-overlay-chain\", \"concept\": \"Nested / decoy overlays: several magic hits, earlier decoy overlay with a bad hash, payload that is itself an ELF or another overlay\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"'Find the FINAL PK19 overlay' implies the generator knows multiple overlays. Fixtures: (a) two PK19 blocks, first with a wrong sha256 (decoy), (b) a magic string inside .rodata (code that checks it) before the real overlay, (c) unpacked payload = a tiny ELF whose own overlay/HCFG holds the config, (d) overlay inside the overlay. Rule set: prefer the LAST magic whose hash verifies; recurse into a payload that starts with a known magic (ELF/PE/NEKO/PK19/RS20/zlib) up to depth 4; report layer count and per-layer offsets (overlay_offset stays the outer file offset unless the question says otherwise).\"},\n349\t  {\"id\": \"decoder-stub-emulation\", \"concept\": \"Find the unpacking stub in code and emulate it over the overlay when the question does NOT spell the transform (timed mutations)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"D19 prompt: 'Find the stub, watch it work ... statically'. The question spelled ror8(b^k2,3)^k1, but a mutated variant may only say 'unpack the overlay'. Locate: code that reads the file (/proc/self/exe open + lseek(end)/fseek) or references the magic constant (cmp dword, 0x39314b50 = 'PK19' LE), then a byte loop with xor/ror/rol/add/sub immediates; extract the op sequence with capstone (xor reg8, imm / ror reg8, imm / xor with a header byte loaded from [buf+5]) and replay it in Python, or emulate the loop with unicorn over the packed bytes (no syscalls: stub the reads). GnuCOBOL stubs are C-library calls (libcob arithmetic) -> fall back to the known-plaintext search: out[0:4]=='HCFG', out[4]==1, u16 out[6:8] == packed_len-12, over transform families {xor a; rot r; xor c} x {add/sub} x {index-dependent}; accept only with the header sha256.\"},\n350\t  {\"id\": \"cobol-gnucobol-deep-facts\", \"concept\": \"GnuCOBOL facts for the d19 group when its theme/identity is backfilled: libcob version, program-id, source file, NEEDED list, cob_* imports, COBOL runtime boolean\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"D19 member (cached: challenges/day19/binary-jack-in-the-box/single_solve/work/extracted/evidence/d19--variant-000.elf): stripped dynamic ELF, NEEDED libcob.so.1, libm.so.6, libvbisam.so.1, libgmp.so.10, libncurses.so.5, libtinfo.so.5, libdl.so.2, libc.so.6; imports cob_init, cob_save_call_params, cob_call_params, cob_check_version, cob_set_programid, cob_push_call_stack_list, cob_stop_run, cob_initialized, cob_fatal_error, cob_cmp, cob_display, cob_get_environment, cob_current_module, cob_unifunc; `.rodata` strings `1.5.2` (cob_check_version arg), `variant-000.cob` (source), host models, `HUNTRESS_HOST_MODEL`, trace family `cobol_static_unpack_trace`, effects `memory_only_inert_payload_hash`, branches failure/decoy/success with event counts 1/17/22/39. Facts keys: has_cobol_runtime (true/false), cobol_runtime_version, source_file, program_id (cob_set_programid argument via the lea before the call), needed, imports. Copy the member into tests/data/binary_fixtures as the fixture; `apt gnucobol3` (3.2) is available for a second, newer-libcob fixture (libcob.so.4).\"},\n351\t  {\"id\": \"haxe-vm-targets\", \"concept\": \"Haxe family beyond Neko: HashLink bytecode (`HLB`), hxcpp native ELF, nekotools-booted executables\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"If Neko lands, the same Haxe source may come as other targets (a pair day: `-neko`/`-hl`, or 'one source, two VMs'). With haxe installed (apt haxe 4.3.7): `haxe -main Main -hl out.hl` (HashLink magic `HLB` + version u8; strings table holds the HCFG), `-neko out.n`, and `nekotools boot out.n` (ELF neko VM + bytecode appended; the bytecode overlay begins with `NEKO`, boot trailer `NEKO` + u32 offset at the end). Facts: format candidates (`hashlink_bytecode`? read the enum), string tables, HCFG offsets. hxcpp (needs g++ + haxelib hxcpp) only if quick.\"},\n352\t  {\"id\": \"packer-decompressors\", \"concept\": \"Decompressors used by real packers for overlay payloads: aPLib, LZNT1, LZMA raw/LZMA86, LZ4 block, LZSS/LZ77 custom, RLE/PackBits\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"A 'static unpacking' sequel (RS20 or Mastery mutations) may compress before the byte transform. Implement pure-Python aPLib (depack), LZNT1, LZSS (4096 ring, 0x20 fill), PackBits/RLE and LZ4 block (python lz4 installed) in lib.binary with try-order by magic/entropy; lzma.FORMAT_RAW with lc3/lp0/pb2 dict 64 KB for raw LZMA. Fixtures: compress an HCFG with each (aPLib via a Python packer implementation), wrap in an overlay header with sha256, assert round-trip + hcfg_find on the output.\"},\n353\t  {\"id\": \"elf-notes-custom-storage\", \"concept\": \"HCFG stored in a custom ELF note (SHT_NOTE `.note.<vendor>` / PT_NOTE): namesz/descsz/type parsing with 4/8 alignment\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Fixture: gcc ELF with `objcopy --add-section .note.huntress=note.bin --set-section-flags .note.huntress=alloc,readonly` (+ a PT_NOTE variant via linker script). Parser: pyelftools iter_notes + raw fallback walking (namesz, descsz, type) with alignment. Expose note owners/types JSON in table order, the desc offset of the HCFG (offset convention: the `H`), has_<owner>_note.\"},\n354\t  {\"id\": \"compressed-elf-sections\", \"concept\": \"SHF_COMPRESSED sections (Elf64_Chdr ch_type 1 zlib / 2 zstd) and legacy `.zdebug_*` (`ZLIB` + u64be size) holding the HCFG\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Fixtures: `objcopy --add-section .hcfg=blob --compress-debug-sections` does not touch non-debug sections, so write Chdr + zlib manually (ch_type, ch_size, ch_addralign) and set SHF_COMPRESSED (0x800); also a `.zdebug_hcfg` legacy one. Decoder: python zlib; zstd needs `pip install zstandard` into .venv (missing) or the `zstd` CLI. Expose compressed size, uncompressed size (ch_size), ch_type label.\"},\n355\t  {\"id\": \"haskell-ghc-deep-facts\", \"concept\": \"GHC + RS20 facts for the d20 group when its theme/identity is backfilled: GHC version, hsLibs/UnitLinkOpts, Main_main closures, has_ghc_runtime, rts options; RS20 header fields\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Fixtures: copy the cached d20 members (single variant-000 + TT/Mastery variants under challenges/day20/binary-resourceful/*/). Facts: ghc_version from the `9.12.2`-style string near `ProjectVersion`/hsLibs (`-lHSghc-internal-9.1202.0`), base version 4.21.0.0, NEEDED [libm, libgmp, libc], `.debug-ghc-link-info` present, gold-version note, symbol count of `_closure`/`_info`, Main module symbols, trace family `haskell_resource_overlay_trace` / effects `private_scratch_hash_only`; RS20: version 1, res_len 380, scratch_len 35, scratch_sha256, scratch text, image_end, overlay_size (463). Expose as facts dict keys matching likely field names.\"},\n356\t  {\"id\": \"pe-certificate-overlay\", \"concept\": \"PE overlay coexisting with an Authenticode certificate table (Security directory points into the file tail), PE checksum, overlay start vs cert range\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"If the storage arc moves to PE (d02/d04/d10 already re-roll PE in Mastery): overlay start = max(PointerToRawData+SizeOfRawData); DIRECTORY_ENTRY_SECURITY VirtualAddress is a FILE offset; HCFG may sit after the WIN_CERTIFICATE (dwLength, wRevision 0x0200, wCertificateType 2) or inside its padding. Fixtures: MinGW PE (x86_64-w64-mingw32-gcc if present, else pefile-synthesized) + fake WIN_CERTIFICATE + appended blob; fields overlay_offset, certificate_offset/size, checksum valid?\"},\n357\t  {\"id\": \"js-runtime-single-executable\", \"concept\": \"Node SEA / Deno compile / Bun --compile / pkg single executables: locate the embedded JS + resources by note/section/trailer\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Node SEA: ELF note/section `NODE_SEA_BLOB` (postject) + fuse string `NODE_SEA_FUSE_fce680ab2cc467b6e072b8b5df1996b2:1`; Deno: trailer `d3n0l4nd` + u64 offsets at EOF; Bun: `\\\\n---- Bun! ----\\\\n` trailer with module graph; pkg: `PAYLOAD_POSITION`/`PRELUDE_POSITION` placeholders. Fixtures can be synthetic (small ELF + trailer layout) since real ones are ~100 MB. Expose embedded_source offset/size, entry name; HCFG via hcfg_scan on the JS text.\"},\n358\t  {\"id\": \"pe-dll-loader-plugin-pair\", \"concept\": \"The D21 shape re-rolled to Windows: loader .exe + plugin .dll (MinGW/MSVC), export directory (names, ordinals, forwarders), import directory, delay-load imports, LoadLibrary/GetProcAddress handshake, DLL side-loading\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"ELF/PE re-rolled per member in Mastery on D2/D4/D10, so a loader/plugin pair may come as PE. lib.binary.pe_link_facts(data): machine (integer and label), characteristics DLL flag, exports [(ordinal, name, rva, forwarder)], import DLLs + functions in directory order, delay imports, TLS callbacks; config in an exported data symbol or .rsrc. Fixtures: x86_64-w64-mingw32-gcc if installed, else synthetic PE via lief with an export table and a .hcfg section; check pefile ordinals base.\"},\n359\t  {\"id\": \"tls-ifunc-loader-facts\", \"concept\": \"Loader-time code paths: PT_TLS/.tdata/.tbss (TLS initializers holding config), STT_GNU_IFUNC resolvers + IRELATIVE relocs, .init_array/.preinit_array order, DT_INIT/DT_FINI, constructor priorities\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"'loader's handshake' read literally. Facts: tls_size/tls_align, tdata bytes (HCFG may sit in .tdata), ifunc symbols + resolver targets (emulate the resolver with unicorn returning a function pointer), init_array entries resolved to symbols in order (RELATIVE addends in PIE!). Extend the built init-time-decoder for ifunc/TLS. Fixtures: gcc __thread char cfg[] = {...}; __attribute__((ifunc)); __attribute__((constructor(101))).\"},\n360\t  {\"id\": \"dwarf-deep-facts\", \"concept\": \"DWARF debug info as answers: CU names and DW_AT_language, DW_AT_producer, comp_dir, subprogram names with low_pc/high_pc, line-table file list, variable/type names (config struct field names)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"D21's loader shipped `with debug_info` (OCaml 4.02.3) and D5 Rust had .debug_*; a 'Debug' / 'symbols beyond the symtab' day is plausible. lib.binary.dwarf_facts(data) via pyelftools: cus [(name, language token as llvm-dwarfdump prints e.g. DW_LANG_C11, producer)], functions (JSON), files (JSON line-table order), DWARF version; also .debug_* compressed (SHF_COMPRESSED) handling (built compressed-elf-sections). Fixtures: gcc -g -gdwarf-4/-5, clang-18 -g.\"},\n361\t  {\"id\": \"native-extension-bridges\", \"concept\": \"Script-runtime native extensions as the native side of an FFI bridge: CPython extension `.so` (PyInit_<mod>, PyModuleDef + PyMethodDef table name/flags/doc), Cython (`__pyx_` symbols, embedded .pyx path), ctypes callers (`CDLL(\\\"libx.so\\\")`, argtypes/restype in .pyc constants), cffi (`_cffi_types`), Node N-API `.node` (napi_register_module_v1, node_register_module_v*), Lua `luaopen_<name>`, Ruby `Init_<name>`\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"lib.binary.extension_bridge_facts(data): kind token (python_ext/cython/napi/lua_c/ruby_ext/plain_c), module name from the init export, method table walk via RELATIVE relocs on PyMethodDef[] (name ptr, fn ptr, flags) until NULL, and for a .pyc partner list ctypes library strings + function names. Fixtures: gcc -shared with Python.h (python3-dev present?) else hand-written PyMethodDef struct; N-API shape via plain C exports; Lua shape via luaopen_ export.\"},\n362\t  {\"id\": \"dotnet-language-family\", \"concept\": \"Other languages on the .NET runtime as a new-day member and their identity facts: VB.NET (Microsoft.VisualBasic ref, `My` namespace, `_Closure$__`, `VB$` locals), F# (SEEN D22: FSharp.Core AssemblyRef, FSharpSignatureData/OptimizationData.<asm> resources, `$Program`/<StartupCode$...> types, `<>f__AnonymousType<n>`, closures `name@<line>`), C++/CLI, IronPython/PowerShell-compiled\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"lib.binary.dotnet_language_of(data) -> token (csharp/fsharp/vbnet/cppcli) with evidence + language facts dict (FSharp.Core version from AssemblyRef and from the dependency member's AssemblyDef, F# resource names, closure count). Fixtures: `dotnet new console -lang VB` and `-lang F#` (dotnet installed); confirm format pe_cli / machine i386 stay unchanged and HCFG scan hits the F# .text array blob first.\"},\n363\t  {\"id\": \"dotnet-primary-support-router\", \"concept\": \"Managed groups with several .dll/.json members: pick the PRIMARY assembly ('primary managed assembly ... dependency DLL members are delivery support only'), expose support-member facts (runtimeconfig tfm/framework name+version, deps.json targets/libraries, dependency AssemblyDef name/version/public key token) and AssemblyRef<->dependency version matching\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Rule: primary = the .dll whose AssemblyDef name is not a framework/dependency name (FSharp.Core, System.*, Microsoft.*, Newtonsoft.*, netstandard) AND that has an entry point or HCFG; tie-break by the question's basename rule. Never scan the 5.7 MB FSharp.Core for HCFG beyond the cheap raw pass. Fixtures: F# console publish output (sample.dll + FSharp.Core.dll + runtimeconfig + deps.json) and a C# app with a ProjectReference library dll.\"},\n364\t  {\"id\": \"mixed-mode-native-in-managed\", \"concept\": \"Native code inside or carried by a managed assembly: C++/CLI mixed-mode PE (COR20 ILONLY clear, VTableFixups, native .text alongside IL, machine x86-64/i386 + 32BITREQUIRED), ReadyToRun native code, and shellcode byte[] executed via VirtualAlloc/mmap + Marshal.Copy + GetDelegateForFunctionPointer\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Facts: cor20 flags tokens, vtfixup count/entries, has_native_code; locate a byte[] initialiser (InitializeArray blob) whose callers reach VirtualAlloc/mprotect P/Invokes, disassemble it with capstone in the PE's machine mode and emulate with unicorn for return constants or an HCFG builder. Fixtures: C# with an x86-64 `mov eax, imm; ret` byte[] run through VirtualAlloc/mmap P/Invoke; mixed-mode only synthetically (pefile flag patch) since MSVC is unavailable.\"},\n365\t  {\"id\": \"reflection-dynamic-load\", \"concept\": \"Reflection / dynamic loading of a second managed or JVM module: Assembly.Load(byte[]) of a resource or array (Costura.Fody `costura.<name>.dll.compressed` raw-deflate resources, AppDomain.AssemblyResolve), Activator/MethodInfo.Invoke by string name; JVM ClassLoader.defineClass of an embedded (xor/zip) class\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"lib.binary.embedded_modules(data): enumerate .NET ManifestResources + large array blobs, raw-inflate (zlib -15) Costura entries, recognise MZ/BSJB or CAFEBABE payloads, recurse the normal facts + HCFG scan on each with a provenance path; report the reflective call strings (type/method names in #US). Fixtures: dotnet console app embedding a second compiled dll as a resource (deflate) loaded with Assembly.Load; a jar with an xor'd .bin class loaded by defineClass.\"},\n366\t  {\"id\": \"dotnet-anti-tamper-obfuscation\", \"concept\": \".NET protector artefacts: SuppressIldasmAttribute, renamed/unprintable metadata names, encrypted method bodies restored in <Module>.cctor (anti-tamper), invalid metadata tricks (extra #~ streams, bogus table rows), ConfusedByAttribute / Dotfuscator / .NET Reactor markers\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"dnfile tolerates most invalid metadata; ilspycmd may crash. Facts: obfuscator name (attribute/marker string), has_suppress_ildasm, renamed_types count, cctor_decrypts_bodies (method RVA bodies with high entropy / zero-length IL). The HCFG must still be found by the raw scan or after the cctor decrypt (emulate the xor loop over the method bodies). de4dot is missing (needs mono) -- note it as a tool gap; keep everything pure Python.\"},\n367\t  {\"id\": \"env-keyed-hcfg-derivation\", \"concept\": \"Environment-keyed config: the HCFG (or its xor key) is decrypted only on the 'true' branch, with a key derived from an env value / host model / hostname (xor with the literal, crc32/fnv/sha256 of it, first byte, length)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"'Force the truth out' suggests a payload unlockable only by the right environment. The candidate keyspace is the binary's OWN compared literals (workstation/analysis/sandbox, the env var name, campaign-like strings): for each literal try xor(literal repeated), sha256(literal)[:n], crc32(literal) bytes, fnv1a32 as key streams over high-entropy blobs near the decoder, accept only crc-valid HCFG + JSON. No external brute force. Fixtures: C ELF + C# dll that xor the HCFG with sha256(\\\"workstation\\\").\"},\n368\t  {\"id\": \"self-modifying-runtime-decrypt\", \"concept\": \"Code or data decrypted in place at runtime (mprotect/VirtualProtect to RWX, xor loop over a function body or .data, then call) -- recover statically by emulation\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Cues: mprotect/VirtualProtect/VirtualAlloc imports, a RWE PT_LOAD or a writable .text, a high-entropy function. Build: find the decrypt loop (capstone xrefs to the protected range), emulate it with unicorn over a copy of the image mapped at its VAs (stub out the syscalls), then run hcfg_scan and the leaf-constant/disassembly extractors on the decrypted bytes. Fixtures: gcc ELF with a function xor-encrypted post-link (python patch) and an mprotect+xor stub.\"},\n369\t  {\"id\": \"custom-bytecode-vm-recovery\", \"concept\": \"Custom bytecode VM obfuscation: interpreter loop + opcode handler table + bytecode blob; the config/predicates live in the VM program\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Next step of the obfuscation family (VMProtect-lite). Cues: a big switch/jump table in a loop reading a byte pointer, a blob with low-cardinality opcode bytes, handlers that push/pop a virtual stack. Build: jumptable recovery (prebuilt) -> map each handler to a semantic (push imm, xor, add, store, jmp, cmp) by emulating each handler in unicorn on a probe state, then a Python interpreter for the blob that logs stores -> hcfg_scan the output buffer. Fixtures: a 10-opcode C VM whose program writes the HCFG bytes.\"},\n370\t  {\"id\": \"crypto-constant-fingerprint-facts\", \"concept\": \"Identify crypto/hash/checksum algorithms by their constants as answer fields (algorithm names list, constant offsets): AES S-box/Te tables, SHA-1/SHA-256/SHA-512 IVs and K, MD5 T, CRC32 0xedb88320 table, TEA/XTEA 0x9e3779b9, ChaCha 'expand 32-byte k', RC4 KSA, FNV/djb2/murmur seeds, Base64 alphabets\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"An analyst-style question ('which cipher does the decoder use') is cheap for the organizers on an obfuscation day. Build a yara/py constant table (little- and big-endian, also inside .NET array blobs and JVM constant pools) returning [(algorithm, offset, encoding)]; facts crypto_algorithms (sorted JSON), has_<alg>_constants booleans. Fixtures: tiny C programs linking each constant set; check against the existing aes-tea-chacha fixtures.\"},\n371\t  {\"id\": \"runtime-codegen-emit-facts\", \"concept\": \"Code generated at runtime: .NET System.Reflection.Emit (DynamicMethod, ILGenerator.Emit opcode sequences, AssemblyBuilder), Expression.Compile, JVM MethodHandles/LambdaMetafactory/defineHiddenClass, native JIT buffers (mmap RWX + memcpy of an opcode array)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"The emitted IL/opcodes exist only as data: recover the Emit call sequence (OpCodes.<X> field loads + operands) from the IL and rebuild the method body; for native, find the opcode byte array copied into an RWX mapping and disassemble it with capstone. Facts: has_runtime_codegen, emitted_opcodes (JSON), emitted constant. Fixtures: a C# DynamicMethod returning a constant; a C program that memcpy's `b8 imm32 c3` into mmap(PROT_EXEC).\"},\n372\t  {\"id\": \"exception-handler-control-flow\", \"concept\": \"Control flow hidden in exception/signal handling: SEH/VEH handlers, int3/ud2 + SIGTRAP/SIGILL handlers (anti-debug), C++ landing pads in .gcc_except_table, .NET try/filter/fault clauses, JVM exception tables that carry the real path\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Anti-debug classic: raise int3 and continue only in the handler when no debugger is attached. Build: parse .eh_frame/.gcc_except_table (pyelftools) call-site tables -> landing pads; PE .pdata/.xdata + VEH registrations (AddVectoredExceptionHandler); .NET method EH clauses (dnfile method body headers); JVM Code attribute exception_table. Facts: handler list with ranges, signal numbers passed to signal/sigaction. Fixtures: gcc C++ throw/catch, C with sigaction(SIGTRAP), C# try/filter.\"},\n373\t  {\"id\": \"de4dot\", \"concept\": \"ConfuserEx / .NET string encryption\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"tool\", \"detail\": \"github de4dot-cex (ViRb3) release; needs apt mono-runtime. `de4dot F -o clean.dll` then ilspycmd.\"},\n374\t  {\"id\": \"erlang-lua-decompilers\", \"concept\": \"BEAM, Lua, LuaJIT bytecode\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"tool\", \"detail\": \"luac (lua5.4) is now installed. Still missing: apt erlang-base (beam_lib/beam_disasm), unluac jar (sourceforge), luajit-decompiler-v2 (github marsinator358) -- only if a bytecode container appears.\"},\n375\t  {\"id\": \"binutils-multiarch\", \"concept\": \"objdump/readelf for MIPS/PPC/SPARC/RISC-V\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"tool\", \"detail\": \"apt install binutils-multiarch; rizin, llvm-objdump-18 and Ghidra already cover disassembly, so this is a convenience only.\"},\n376\t  {\"id\": \"ihex-srec-firmware\", \"concept\": \"Intel HEX / S-record / raw firmware members\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"note\", \"detail\": \"objcopy -I ihex|srec -O binary already converts (srecord not needed). For raw blobs: rizin -a arm -b 16 -m <base>; format label unknown (`ihex`/`srec`/`raw`?) -> submit alone.\"},\n377\t  {\"id\": \"dart-aot-snapshot\", \"concept\": \"Dart AOT executable (`dart compile exe`): snapshot sections, HCFG inside the isolate snapshot (possibly compressed/obfuscated)\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Cues: `_kDartVmSnapshotData`, `_kDartIsolateSnapshotData/Instructions` symbols, `Dart_` runtime strings, ELF appended to dartaotruntime (or a standalone ELF in recent SDKs). Strings in the snapshot are stored as OneByteString objects (raw latin-1 with header) -> raw scan works unless compressed pointers/obfuscation; fallback search for SENGR base64. Record snapshot hash (32 hex) as a possible provenance field. No Dart SDK installed: synthesize an ELF with those symbols + OneByteString-shaped blob.\"},\n378\t  {\"id\": \"backfill-language-identity-facts\", \"concept\": \"Per-language identity + theme facts for the D8-D17 groups (the next backfill): has_<lang>_runtime / has_<lang>_mangled_symbol / class, protocol, selector, proc, template names\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"BUILT (prebuild-state ok). D17 re-asked D1-D7's single-solve facts on their old groups (marker, recover_code, mangled_score_symbol, typeinfo_symbol, has_go_runtime, has_rust_mangled_symbol, methods, access_flags, method_count, ...\"},\n379\t  {\"id\": \"jvm-classfile-facts\", \"concept\": \"Full JVM ClassFile facts for jar groups (d06/d07): versions, constant-pool count, this/super/interfaces, fields, methods+descriptors, attributes, Kotlin metadata\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"BUILT (prebuild-state ok). D17 asked methods (names, table order, incl <init>), access_flags (decimal 49) and method_count (incl <init>/<clinit>) of the Main-Class. Next backfill may ask major_version/minor_version, constant_pool_count, ...\"},\n380\t  {\"id\": \"dotnet-metadata-facts\", \"concept\": \".NET metadata facts for the d03 group: assembly name/version, MVID, TypeDef/MethodDef names, FieldRVA, TargetFramework, entry point token\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"BUILT (prebuild-state ok). d03 is the only old group whose day-facts were not re-asked on D17 (it got hcfg_version/xor_key_hex only); a later backfill likely asks typedef/method names, method_count, assembly_name, assembly_version, ...\"},\n381\t  {\"id\": \"decoder-routine-locator\", \"concept\": \"Locate and characterise the config DECODER in the binary: function name, algorithm (xor/add/rol/rc4...), key/immediate, loop length, references to the stored blob\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"BUILT (prebuild-state ok). D17 prompt: 'Recover the reversible decoder' (unasked, but a later backfill may ask decoder facts on d17 or any HCFG group). From the validated HcfgHit: compute blob VA, find code xrefs (RIP-relative lea/mov to VA in ...\"},\n382\t  {\"id\": \"provenance-facts-extractor\", \"concept\": \"Build provenance fields: GNU build-id, .comment compiler banner, DWARF producer/language/comp_dir, PE TimeDateStamp/PDB path/Rich, Go/Rust toolchain version\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"BUILT (prebuild-state ok). Implement in the facts dict so a new id answers without code: build_id = lowercase hex of NT_GNU_BUILD_ID desc (no 0x), compiler = first `.comment` string, dwarf_producer via pyelftools, pdb_path from RSDS, timestamp as ...\"},\n383\t  {\"id\": \"language-detector\", \"concept\": \"lib.binary.language_of(data) -> source language/toolchain token with evidence, for all 17 seen languages + next candidates\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"BUILT (prebuild-state ok). A `language`/`compiler`/`toolchain` id on any group would need consistent tokens: c, cpp, csharp/dotnet, go, rust, java, kotlin, swift, nim, zig, d, pascal/fpc, crystal, objc, wat/wasm, ada; candidates haskell, ocaml, ...\"},\n384\t  {\"id\": \"emulate-return-value\", \"concept\": \"Recover a function's return value by emulation when it is not a `mov eax, imm; ret` leaf (obfuscated/computed/OLLVM recover_code)\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"BUILT (prebuild-state ok). recover_code was re-asked D17; a mutated variant may compute the constant (xor of two imms, lookup table, flattened switch). unicorn x86-64 (installed): map the ELF PT_LOADs, set rsp to a scratch stack, run from the ...\"},\n385\t  {\"id\": \"api-hashing-resolver\", \"concept\": \"Imports resolved by hash (ROR13, djb2, FNV-1a, CRC32, murmur) -> resolved API list / hash algorithm fields\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"BUILT (prebuild-state ok). Natural 'encoded' sequel to D17 for a decoder-themed day. Precompute hash tables for libc/kernel32/ntdll export names under the common algorithms; scan .rodata/.text immediates (capstone `cmp`/`mov` imm32) and report ...\"},\n386\t  {\"id\": \"per-string-encryption\", \"concept\": \"Every string (not just HCFG) encrypted individually with a shared decoder (xor/add per string, stack strings) -> decoded string lists as fields\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"BUILT (prebuild-state ok). Escalation of the D17 'encoded configuration' theme: config fields stored as separate xor'd strings instead of one HCFG blob. Use floss (installed in .venv) + a capstone pass collecting (ptr,len,key) triples from ...\"},\n387\t  {\"id\": \"build-pair-router\", \"concept\": \"Same-source build PAIRS beyond stripped/symbolized and compact/direct (static/dynamic, O0/O2/Os, pie/nopie, debug/release, packed/unpacked, plain/obfuscated)\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"BUILT (prebuild-state ok). D15 and D16 were both 'one source, two builds' with `dNN_analysis_<tag>_<field>` ids. Fixtures: gcc -O0 vs -O2, -static vs dynamic, -pie vs -no-pie, -g vs stripped, upx'd vs plain, each with a `.hcfg` section and ... D24 SEEN as a vulnerable/corrected twin (Scala jars) -- the generic qualifier peel covered it with zero code.\"},\n388\t  {\"id\": \"cross-arch-pair\", \"concept\": \"Same source built for x86-64 + AArch64 (+ RISC-V/ARM .o) as a pair, arch-named qualifiers\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"BUILT (prebuild-state ok). aarch64-linux-gnu-gcc-15 links, clang-18 --target=riscv64/armv7 -c gives ET_REL. Name tags like `-x86_64.elf`/`-aarch64.elf`/`-arm64` put an UNDERSCORE inside the qualifier (`d17_analysis_x86_64_machine`): the router ...\"},\n389\t  {\"id\": \"wasm-inventory-fields\", \"concept\": \"WASM 'doors' as answer fields: imports, exports, memory min/max/shared/memory64, table + elem (call_indirect targets), start, globals, data segment count/offsets, custom sections\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"BUILT (prebuild-state ok). The D16 prompt named imports/memory/indirect calls but asked none; carry-over backfill may add them. Build fixtures with wat2wasm (installed): imports from env/wasi_snapshot_preview1 (func/memory/table/global), funcref ...\"},\n390\t  {\"id\": \"ebpf-object\", \"concept\": \"eBPF ELF object (e_machine 247) with HCFG in .rodata / a map section\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"BUILT (prebuild-state ok). clang-18 -target bpf -O2 -c fixture with SEC(\\\"xdp\\\"), a `license` section, `.maps`, and an HCFG `.hcfg`/`.rodata` blob. Targets: format `elf`, elf_type ET_REL, machine readelf spelling `Linux BPF` (EM_BPF; integer 247), ...\"},\n391\t  {\"id\": \"sstrip-corrupt-headers\", \"concept\": \"ELF without section headers (sstrip, e_shnum=0) or with bogus e_shoff/e_shstrndx/fake section names\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"BUILT (prebuild-state ok). Fixtures: gcc build then python-zero e_shoff/e_shnum/e_shstrndx; another with garbage e_shstrndx; another with a section renamed to `.hcfg` that does not hold the blob. Targets: parser never crashes (pyelftools wrapped, ...\"},\n392\t  {\"id\": \"wasm-hcfg-hidden\", \"concept\": \"WASM HCFG not a plain active data segment: custom section `hcfg`, passive segment + memory.init, split across segments, built by i32.store immediates, UTF-16 (AssemblyScript), memory64 module\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"BUILT (prebuild-state ok). Natural Mastery/next-day twist of D16. Fixtures via wat2wasm: (a) custom section named hcfg (has_hcfg_section analogue -> `true`), (b) passive segment, (c) blob split over two active segments at adjacent mem offsets ...\"},\n393\t  {\"id\": \"bytecode-containers\", \"concept\": \"LLVM bitcode, Python .pyc, Lua luac, standalone .class/.dex as group members\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"BUILT (prebuild-state ok). Fixtures: clang-18 -c -emit-llvm (BC C0 DE + wrapper), python -m py_compile (3.x magic), luac (installed), javac single class. Record magic -> candidate format labels (`llvm_bitcode`/`bitcode`, `pyc`, `luac`/`lua`, ...\"},\n394\t  {\"id\": \"dotnet-singlefile-aot\", \"concept\": \".NET single-file bundle, ReadyToRun and NativeAOT builds\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"BUILT (prebuild-state ok). dotnet installed: `dotnet publish -p:PublishSingleFile=true` (apphost + bundle manifest, `.net core bundle` signature hash), `-p:PublishReadyToRun=true` (R2R header in CLI dll), `-p:PublishAot=true` (native ELF, no ...\"},\n395\t  {\"id\": \"upx-packed-hcfg\", \"concept\": \"UPX-packed ELF/PE (plain and with scrubbed UPX! magic / renamed sections)\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"BUILT (prebuild-state ok). Fixture: `upx -9` a C ELF + MinGW PE carrying an HCFG `.hcfg` section; variant with `UPX!` zeroed and UPX0/1 renamed. Target: solver detects (packer_info), restores magic, `upx -d` on a copy, then hcfg_find + header ...\"},\n396\t  {\"id\": \"aes-tea-chacha-hcfg\", \"concept\"