packed PK19 overlay (not a raw/b64 blob; see question-spec-overlay-unpacker); resource parts unseen. Fixtures: MinGW-free path = patch a resource dir with pefile into a small PE; dnfile resource in a dotnet-built dll; jar with config.bin; ELF/PE with blob appended past the last section. Confirm hcfg_scan finds each and ...\"},\n401\t  {\"id\": \"rolling-xor-hcfg\", \"concept\": \"Index-dependent xor (key+i, key^prev, xor with len/crc)\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"BUILT (prebuild-state ok). Extend the bytemap/mxor fixture family: known-plaintext 'HCFG' recovers the start key and step; brute 256 x {add,sub,xor-prev} modes, crc-gate. Not covered by current single-byte or repeating-key ...\"},\n402\t  {\"id\": \"init-time-decoder\", \"concept\": \"Config decoded in .init_array constructor / TLS callback / DllMain\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"BUILT (prebuild-state ok). Fixture with __attribute__((constructor)) decoding a stored blob; extractor finds .init_array targets and emulates them with unicorn (stdlib-free). Low until a day theme hints at runtime ...\"},\n403\t  {\"id\": \"exotic-codecs\", \"concept\": \"base58/base62/base91/z85 and lz4/zstd/brotli HCFG\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"BUILT (prebuild-state ok). tools/pybase62 + tools/pybase91 + python lz4 exist; pip install zstandard brotli into the venv. Add hcfg_fixtures entries with speculative offset = first stored ...\"},\n404\t  {\"id\": \"direct-syscall-facts\", \"concept\": \"APIs invoked by raw `syscall` instructions instead of imports (static/no-libc binaries): syscall numbers -> names -> intent\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"An 'API intent' / 'prove no injection' sequel can hide process_vm_writev (310), ptrace (101), memfd_create (319), execve (59) behind inline syscalls. Extractor: capstone scan for `syscall` (x86-64) / `svc #0` (AArch64) / `int 0x80` (i386), backward-resolve the eax/x8 immediate, map with the x86-64/aarch64/i386 syscall tables (embed as dicts), feed api-intent-injection-classifier. Fixtures: gcc -nostdlib -static C with inline asm syscalls.\"},\n405\t  {\"id\": \"lisp-scheme-member\", \"concept\": \"Lisp-family native images as a new-day member: SBCL core-embedded executable, Chicken Scheme (csc), Racket `raco exe`, ECL\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Remaining 'unusual runtime' languages after Haskell/OCaml/Fortran. Cues: SBCL huge static ELF with `SBCL` + core appended (`\\\\x00\\\\x00\\\\x00\\\\x00CORE` magic / `--core` strings, `sb-impl::`), Chicken `C_toplevel`, `libchicken.so.11`, `C_` symbols, Racket `.rackboot` section / `racket/base` strings, ECL `libecl.so`. HCFG likely a string literal (raw or base64) inside a heap image: raw/base64 scan must still work; offsets = first stored byte. Build fixtures only if the compilers are apt-installable (`apt-cache policy sbcl chicken-bin racket ecl`).\"},\n406\t  {\"id\": \"erlang-elixir-beam-member\", \"concept\": \"Erlang/Elixir BEAM member: `FOR1....BEAM` IFF chunks (AtU8/Atom, Code, LitT zlib, StrT, ExpT/ImpT) and escripts (shebang + zip)\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Python chunk parser (4-byte id, u32be size, 4-aligned); LitT = u32be uncompressed size + zlib of external-term-format literals -> HCFG likely a binary literal; escript = text header lines + zip (see appended-archive-sfx). format label unknown (not in the enum) -> submit alone. erlang-base apt available for fixtures.\"},\n407\t  {\"id\": \"graalvm-julia-native-image\", \"concept\": \"Heavy AOT images that embed resources: GraalVM native-image (`-H:IncludeResources`, `__svm_` heap), Julia sysimage/PackageCompiler apps\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Cues: GraalVM `com.oracle.svm`, `__svm_vm_target`, `.svm_heap` section, resources stored as byte[] in the image heap (raw HCFG scan likely works); Julia `libjulia`, `jl_` symbols, `sys.so` with `jl_system_image_data`. Fixtures synthetic (section names + blob) unless native-image is installable. Expose has_<runtime>, the section holding the HCFG.\"},\n408\t  {\"id\": \"kernel-module-ko-member\", \"concept\": \"Linux kernel module (.ko, ET_REL) as a member: .modinfo key=value strings (license, author, description, vermagic, depends, name), __versions CRCs, init_module/cleanup_module, .gnu.linkonce.this_module\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"User/kernel is the next 'boundary'; .ko is an ELF64 ET_REL (elf_type ET_REL, entry 0x0, machine 62). Facts: modinfo dict in section order, vermagic, depends list, exported symbols (__ksymtab_*), HCFG in .rodata/.data of the relocatable (raw scan works; offset = file offset). Fixture: synthetic ET_REL with a .modinfo section (no kernel headers needed: gcc -c + objcopy --add-section).\"},\n409\t  {\"id\": \"macho-dylib-pair\", \"concept\": \"Mach-O loader + dylib pair: LC_LOAD_DYLIB / LC_LOAD_WEAK_DYLIB / LC_RPATH (@rpath, @loader_path, @executable_path), LC_ID_DYLIB, exports trie, chained fixups\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"If the pair theme moves to Apple containers (Swift/ObjC were ELF so far; macho label presumed `macho`, prebuilt macho-hcfg-section). lib.binary.macho_link_facts(data) via lief: dylibs in load-command order, rpaths, install name, exported symbols, cputype (integer 16777223 / label x86_64). Fixtures: lief-built Mach-O with a __DATA,__hcfg section and LC_LOAD_DYLIB entries.\"},\n410\t  {\"id\": \"com-interop-typelib\", \"concept\": \"COM as the managed<->native bridge: [ComImport]/[Guid]/[InterfaceType] interfaces in .NET metadata, CLSID/IID strings, Marshal.GetActiveObject/CoCreateInstance P/Invokes, type libraries (`MSFT` .tlb, embedded TYPELIB resource), registration-free COM manifests\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Facts: GUIDs from GuidAttribute custom-attribute blobs, interface method order (vtable slot = index + 3 for IUnknown, +7 for IDispatch), CoCreateInstance CLSID constants, .tlb header parse (MSFT magic, typeinfo count, names). Fixtures: C# console with a [ComImport] interface and Guid attributes (builds on Linux; runtime not needed).\"},\n411\t  {\"id\": \"garble-go-obfuscation\", \"concept\": \"Obfuscated Go builds (garble: hashed package/function names, -literals obfuscated strings, -tiny stripped pclntab file names) on the d04 group or a new member\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Go facts (buildinfo, function names) degrade: buildinfo may be stripped, names hashed (`Z7xk2...`), literals rebuilt by small xor/add closures at init. Build: detect garble (hashed names in pclntab, missing buildinfo deps, `-literals` closure patterns), report has_garble; recover literals by emulating the literal closures (unicorn) or by hcfg_scan over the closure immediates. Fixtures: garble needs a Go toolchain (`go install mvdan.cc/garble@latest`); if Go is absent, record as a tool gap.\"}\n412\t]\n413\t```\n414\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e7b9f74d-13fa-4643-a706-3e89af5c6241","uuid":"3218300b-14a8-4da4-aaab-6d6b4987ac47","timestamp":"2026-10-25T13:08:32.828Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/testpwn/huntress-2026/reference/coverage/binary-reverse-engineering.md","content":"# Coverage atlas -- binary-reverse-engineering (as of D24 post-run, 2026-10-24)\n\nScope: what a D25+ `evidence.zip` group (or backfilled old-group id) could be, how we would recognise it, which standard tool answers it, and how ready we\nare. Grounded in `reference/techniques/binary-reverse-engineering.md` (lane log D1-D24), `challenges/day24/binary-spot-the-difference/solver/` (byte-identical to D23's),\n`lib/binary.py` (`hcfg_scan`/`hcfg_find`, `packer_info`, `unpack_upx`, `go_buildinfo`, `go_pclntab_funcs`, `rustfilt`, `macho_facts`,\n`recover_return_constants`, `ghidra_decompile`, `jar_app_classes`, `wasm_layout`) and `tests/data/binary_fixtures/TARGETS.json` (all 9 targets have fixtures).\n\nProgression so far: D1-D14 = one new compiled language per day (container nearly always ELF64 x86-64, HCFG blob re-stored per\nlanguage); D15-D16 = \"ONE SOURCE, TWO BUILDS\" pairs with a `<qualifier>_` id prefix (`stripped`/`symbolized`, `compact`/`direct`);\nD17 Ada ELF + BACKFILL #2 (160 -> 204 ids: old days' single-solve facts re-asked on their groups + the `hcfg_storage` enum after a\nmid-day contract revision); D18 Fortran ELF (theme \"call graph / no injection\" unasked, CORRECT T+11 s). **D19 \"Jack in the Box\"\n(static-unpacking)** = ONE GnuCOBOL ELF (11 KB, `libcob.so.1`, stripped) whose HCFG is NOT in the image: a `PK19` overlay is\nappended after the section-header table (`PK19|ver|k1|k2|pad|u32le len|sha256[32]|packed`, unpack `ror8(b^k2,3)^k1`, sha256-check,\nHCFG at out[0]). FIRST day whose prompt theme WAS asked on its own group: config_* only after unpacking + NEW `overlay_offset`\n(offset of the last magic) / `overlay_size` (file length - offset). The question text spelled the whole stub; 228 ids = 216 + 12,\nno backfill; CORRECT T+2:25, TT 4 s / Mastery (5 sets) 10 s first try; overlay 10808/424 constant across variants.\n**D20 \"Resourceful\" (resources-and-overlays)** = ONE Haskell ELF (GHC 9.12.2, 1.2 MB, dynamic libgmp, not stripped) + a 463-B\n`RS20` overlay at e_shoff+e_shnum*64: `RS20|ver@4|u32le res_len@8|u16le scratch_len@12|sha256(scratch)@16|HCFG resource@48 (RAW)|\nscratch` (\"private-scratch:<campaign>:inert-only\"). 240 ids = 228 + 12; NEW `hcfg_resource_size` (= u32le @8, 380). The prebuilt\nRS20/question-spec unpacker + raw HCFG scan banked 239 ids at T+27 s; one field branch -> CORRECT T+49 s, 0 wrong; TT 4.8 s /\nMastery 9.3 s first try; overlay constant across variants. D19-D20 = a \"hidden storage\" arc (packed overlay -> resource overlay;\nprompt: \"resources, overlays, bytes past the end of the sections ... map every boundary\").\n**D21 \"Shared Custody\" (shared-library-boundaries)** = a LOADER + PLUGIN pair: `-loader.elf` (780 KB OCaml 4.02.3 native PIE,\ndebug_info, NEEDED libm/libdl/libc, Dynlink `caml_natdynlink_open`/`caml_dlopen`; NO HCFG) + `-plugin.cmxs` (9 KB ET_DYN OCaml\nnatdynlink plugin, exports `caml_plugin_header`/`caml_globals`/`camlPlugin_000*`, `Caml2007D002` dynheader, HCFG RAW in `.data`).\n252 ids = 240 + 12: `loader_machine`/`plugin_machine` (integer 62) + config_* twice (unqualified ids name the plugin IN THE\nQUESTION, plus `plugin_config_*`). The theme (exports/imports/handshake) was NOT asked. Only a routing change (question-named\nmember, applied after the qualifier peel) -> CORRECT T+1:33, 0 wrong; TT 4.2 s / Mastery 9.9 s first try.\n**D22 \"Bridge Troll\" (managed-native-bridge)** = an F# .NET 8 group of 3: `d22--sample.dll` (18.8 KB, PE32 i386 ILONLY, BSJB\n`v4.0.30319`) + `sample.runtimeconfig.json` (same bytes as d03's) + `FSharp.Core.dll` (5.7 MB stock dependency, constant sha256\nacross sets). Bridge = 2 P/Invoke ImplMap rows (`getpid`@ModuleRef `libc`, `GetCurrentProcessId`@`kernel32.dll`, Winapi), trace\n`fsharp_managed_native_bridge_trace`. HCFG RAW in `.text` (F# array blob) + an identical copy as a PE overlay; question: \"first\nrecord that validates\". 264 ids = 252 + 12 (3 sha256 + the d03 field family verbatim); theme NOT asked. All members silently\nrenamed `dNN--variant-000.*` -> `dNN--sample.*`. Carried-over solver -> CORRECT T+47 s, 0 wrong; TT 12.3 s / Mastery (6 sets,\n1584 ids) 18.2 s first try. FIRST day re-using an old RUNTIME with a new language (.NET: C# D3 -> F# D22).\n**D23 \"Trust Issues\" (anti-analysis-recognition)** = a VB.NET .NET 8 group of 2: `d23--sample.dll` (8 KB, PE32 i386 ILONLY,\n.text/.rsrc/.reloc, BSJB `v4.0.30319`, AssemblyRefs System.Runtime/Microsoft.VisualBasic.Core/System.Text.Json/System.Console,\n`StandardModuleAttribute`, `VB$AnonymousType_0`8`) + `sample.runtimeconfig.json` (d03's bytes). Predicates (theme, UNASKED):\n`Debugger.get_IsAttached`, `Stopwatch.StartNew`/`get_ElapsedTicks` (clock), `Environment.get_ProcessorCount`,\n`GetEnvironmentVariable(\"HUNTRESS_HOST_MODEL\")` vs workstation/analysis/sandbox -> branch success/decoy/failure, trace\n`vbnet_anti_analysis_predicate_trace`/`inert_predicate_only`, field `analysis_detected`. No ImplMap, no FieldRVA. HCFG RAW ONCE as\na PE overlay right after `.reloc` (7680 = EOF-380). 276 ids = 264 + 12 (2 sha256 + d22 family + `xor_key_hex`). Carried-over\nsolver -> CORRECT T+84 s (22 s download), 0 wrong; TT 13.0 s / Mastery 7 sets (1932 ids) 7.9 s first try. NEW in timed modes:\nvalue SHAPES re-rolled (`BR23-<8 uppercase hex>` campaign, d01 marker `BR01-<8hex>`, d01 FILE symbol `sample.c`) -- harmless\nfor a verbatim-copying solver. THIRD .NET language (C# D3, F# D22, VB.NET D23) and the first BEHAVIOUR (evasion) theme.\n**D24 \"Spot the Difference\" (patch-diffing)** = a Scala 2.13 TWIN pair: `d24--sample-vulnerable.jar` (member 1) +\n`d24--sample-corrected.jar` (member 2), ~4 KB each, manifest `Created-By: Huntress deterministic Scala factory`, classes\n`Day24<Role>000.class` (static forwarder, Main-Class) + `Day24<Role>000$.class` (module: `MODULE$`, base64 HCFG `ldc` in\n`<clinit>`, `decodeConfig`, `score(String)I`, `main`), `ScalaSignature`/`ScalaSig`, scala-library not bundled. Prompt: \"Two\nbuilds, one fix. Diff the vulnerable function against its corrected twin and pinpoint exactly what changed -- then prove the old\none was really broken.\" The fix (UNASKED): only `score` changed -- vulnerable `if (s.nonEmpty) s.charAt(0) else -1` NPEs on\n`null` (CWE-476); corrected `Option(s).filter(_.nonEmpty).map(_.charAt(0)).getOrElse(-1)` (+3 invokedynamic lambdas). `main`\nidentical (HUNTRESS_HOST_MODEL lookupswitch -> decoy/success/failure), trace `scala_patch_diff_trace`/`benign_control_and_\nreversion_only` + `control_positive`. 288 ids = 276 + 12: 2 sha256, `vulnerable_format`/`corrected_format` (`jar`), 4\nUNQUALIFIED config_* (\"decode both role members, require byte-for-byte equal config, use the common value\"), 4\n`corrected_config_*`. Carried-over solver, ZERO new code -> CORRECT T+35 s, 0 wrong; TT 5.0 s / Mastery 8 sets (2304 ids) 8.4 s\nfirst try. The whole contract was reworded into specs (sha256 \"ZIP central-directory order (1-based)\", HCFG layout + JAR carrier\nrule \"Base64-alphabet UTF-8 constants >= 80 chars\"); timed modes re-shaped domain/mutex/url too (`<word>-<8hex>.dayNN...`,\n`Global\\Huntress<12HEX>`, `/<word>/<10hex>`).\nArc since D18 = one structure/behaviour concept per day: call graph -> packing -> resources/overlays -> shared libraries ->\nmanaged/native bridge -> anti-analysis predicates -> PATCH DIFFING (first \"vulnerability research\" concept). Natural next\n(D25-D31, 7 days left): more vuln-research (bug-class identification, trigger input / crash proof, exploitability facts such\nas buffer size / overwrite distance / canary, symbolic reachability), native or .NET twin pairs (the diff on ELF/PE, possibly\nstripped), patch FILES (bsdiff/IPS/xdelta) applied to a base, the rest of the evasion family (string encryption, anti-disasm,\nCFF/opaque predicates, self-modifying code, custom VM, API hashing), crypto-constant recognition, FFI on other runtimes, more\n\"new language on an old runtime\" (Clojure/Groovy JVM -- D26 leak --, C++/CLI, Elixir, Haxe->Neko), and a theme backfill.\n**Forward hints still open**: `neko_bytecode` in the format enum (unseen through D24); d07 `method_count` text: \"for Day 26 use the\nprimary classfile named by that unit\" (=> a JVM classfile member on D26 whose primary class is named by the question, not the\nmanifest -- D24's Scala `Foo$` module shows why: the Main-Class is only a forwarder). No new magic token / day number in the\nD20-D24 contracts (D22 reworded basenames, D24 reworded every question into a spec): next twist unannounced.\nLessons for D21+: (a) read the longest question of each new family first -- it is the layout spec; (b) every `*_size`/`*_offset`/\n`*_sha256` id maps to ONE named header field: parse the spec into a struct and expose every field; (c) grep each contract for\ntokens/days that are not today's; (d) header ids of the new member are answered by the carried-over solver; the twist is the new\nfield family; (e) `none` only for ABSENT things; (f) unguessable labels get fixed by contract revision -- re-pull; (g) D21: the\nQUESTION can name the member for an unqualified id (\"Use the d21-- plugin.cmxs member\") -- route on the text after the id peel;\n(h) D22: a group shaped like an old group inherits that group's field family; extra `.dll`s are \"delivery support only\" -- pick\nthe PRIMARY assembly, never key on `variant-` in basenames (renamed to `sample`), and keep FIRST-valid-HCFG semantics;\n(i) D23: a behaviour theme (anti-analysis) on a must-not-run binary was still answered statically (header + HCFG); timed modes\nre-shaped VALUES (`BRNN-<8hex>`) -- copy values verbatim, never validate their shape; (j) D24: a twin pair adds `<role>_`\nqualifiers BEFORE the field family plus unqualified ids defined as the CONSENSUS of both members (decode all, assert equal);\nScala logic lives in the `$` module class, not the Main-Class forwarder.\nAsked field names: config_*, format (enum), machine, architecture, elf_class, elf_type, endianness, entry_point, symbols,\nsection_names, disassembly, marker, recover_code, has_symtab, has_cpp_*, has_go_runtime, has_rust_mangled_symbol,\nhas_coroutine_runtime, mangled_score_symbol, typeinfo_symbol, methods, access_flags, method_count, has_hcfg_section, hcfg_offset,\nhcfg_version, hcfg_storage (enum), xor_key_hex, metadata_version, compression_methods, overlay_offset, overlay_size,\nhcfg_resource_size, `<role>_machine` (D21 loader/plugin, integer), `<role>_format` + `<role>_config_*` (D24 vulnerable/corrected).\nRemaining risks: (000) the D24 diff asked as fields (changed method name/descriptor, bug class / CWE, trigger input, outcome\nper build) or a NATIVE twin pair whose diff must be found by function matching (stripped?) -- see the patch-diff gaps; (00) the D23 predicates asked as fields (predicate list, env var name, compared host-model values, branch per\nhost model, timing threshold, `analysis_detected` verdict) or an obfuscation sequel (encrypted strings/IL, anti-disassembly,\nflattened control flow) where the HCFG is only reachable through a decoder; (0) the bridge theme backfilled on d22 (ImplMap module/import names, callconv, marshaled types, call sites) or\nan FFI bridge on another runtime (JNI, ctypes, N-API) with a native member; (1) the structure arc continues (linking internals:\nrelocations/GOT/PLT, symbol versions, RPATH/RUNPATH, TLS/IFUNC, or a PE DLL loader/plugin pair) with 2+ role members -- route by question text; (2) a backfill of the D18-D21 themes\n(call graph, PK19/RS20 header fields, NEEDED/exports/dlopen target/plugin header); (3) Neko bytecode labels (VM machine/arch);\n(4) D26 JVM classfile member; (5) per-language fact backfills (D8-D21 groups); (6) a 3+-member group (loader + several plugins,\ndecoy HCFG in the loader).\n\nTool legend: **[I]** installed (`source bin/env.sh`; checked with `which`/`ls`), **[M]** missing.\nInstalled: readelf/objdump/nm/c++filt/strings/objcopy (binutils x86-64 + aarch64-linux-gnu-objdump), llvm-18 (llvm-objdump-18,\nllvm-readobj-18, llvm-otool, llvm-lipo, llvm-nm, llvm-dwarfdump, llvm-cxxfilt-18 under /usr/lib/llvm-18/bin), file, binwalk, upx 4.2.4,\nrizin 0.9.1 (`bin/rizin`, `rz-bin`, `rz-asm`, `rz-find`, `rz-diff`) + radare2/rabin2, Ghidra (`bin/analyzeHeadless`, processors incl.\nAARCH64/ARM/MIPS/PowerPC/RISCV/Sparc/x86/JVM/Dalvik), GoReSym, rustfilt, swift-demangle, nim-demangle, ilspycmd, dotnet, java/javap,\njadx, dex2jar, apktool, pyinstxtractor, pycdc/pycdas, autoit-ripper, hbc-decompiler, gdb + gdb-multiarch, ltrace/strace, yara, wabt (wasm-objdump/wasm2wat/wat2wasm/wasm-decompile), floss (.venv), luac,\n7z, xxd; venv python: capstone, unicorn, angr, lief, pyelftools, pefile, dnfile, pycryptodome, pyzipper, xdis/uncompyle6/decompyle3,\nlz4, yara. Cross compilers: aarch64-linux-gnu-gcc-15, clang-18 (no lld/wasm-ld: other targets compile to `.o` only).\nMissing: qemu-user(-static), wasm-ld/lld, wasmtime, capa, Detect-It-Easy (diec), de4dot, monodis, erlang (beam_disasm),\nunluac/luajit-decompiler (luac present), blutter, srecord (srec_cat), binutils-multiarch, checksec, python zstandard/brotli, rzpipe/r2pipe.\n\n## Concept table\n\n| # | concept | status | recognition cues | standard tool + exact command | D20+ likelihood |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 1 | C ELF (gcc, glibc) | seen D1, D15 (+ every day's d01; D17 re-asked marker/recover_code) | `GCC: (...)` in `.comment`, `.interp` ld-linux, `__libc_start_main` | [I] `readelf -hSW f; readelf -sW f; objdump -d -M intel f` | high (carry-over every day; mastery d01 re-rolls stripped/renamed) |\n| 2 | C++ Itanium ELF / MinGW PE32+ | seen D2 | `_Z` symbols, `_ZTV`/`_ZTI`/`_ZTS`, `libstdc++`; PE `.text$_Z...` COMDAT, `.CRT`, `.tls` | [I] `nm -C f`; `objdump -t f.exe`; `c++filt` | high (carry-over; ELF/PE re-rolls per member) |\n| 3 | .NET C# / F# / VB.NET PE (pe_cli) | seen D3 (C#), D22 (F#: FSharp.Core dependency member), **D23 (VB.NET: `Microsoft.VisualBasic.Core` AssemblyRef, `StandardModuleAttribute`, `VB$AnonymousType_N`; 8 KB, HCFG RAW only as PE overlay)** -- labels identical (`pe_cli`/`i386`/`v4.0.30319`) | `BSJB` metadata root `v4.0.30319`, `mscoree.dll`/`_CorExeMain`, `.runtimeconfig.json` | [I] `ilspycmd f.dll`; python `dnfile` | high (carry-over; a 4th .NET language -- C++/CLI, PowerShell-hosted, IronPython -- possible) |\n| 4 | Go (static, stripped; PE in Mastery) | seen D4 | `\\xff Go buildinf:`, `.gopclntab`, `runtime.`, `go1.NN` | [I] `GoReSym -t -d -p f`; `go version -m f`; `lib.binary.go_buildinfo` | high (carry-over) |\n| 5 | Rust ELF (debug_info) | seen D5 | `_ZN...17h<16hex>E` / `_R` v0 symbols, `rustc version`, `/rustc/<sha>/library` panic paths | [