{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_012YVUNKKf7Qjmo2FzBHWetP","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# binary-reverse-engineering — technique log (days 1-25; updated after every day)\n2\t\n3\tHow this lane has looked so far (OBSERVATIONS, not guarantees):\n4\t- **Timed variants MUTATE** (organizer, D8: \"new, dynamic variations/mutations\"): solvers derive structure, degrade per field.\n5\t- One `evidence.zip` (AES, password `infected`), CUMULATIVE from D3: one group per past day (`dNN--variant-XXX.<ext>`, renamed\n6\t  `dNN--sample.<ext>` since D22) + ONE new container/language per day: D1 C ELF, D2 C++ (ELF or MinGW PE32+), D3 .NET, D4 Go,\n7\t  D5 Rust, D6 Java jar, D7 Kotlin jar, D8 Swift (67 MB), D9 Nim, D10 Zig (PE in Mastery), D11 D, D12 Free Pascal, D13 Crystal,\n8\t  D14 ObjC, D15 C pair `-stripped`/`-symbolized`, D16 WASM pair `-compact`/`-direct`, D17 Ada, D18 Fortran, D19 GnuCOBOL + `PK19`\n9\t  packed overlay, D20 Haskell + `RS20` overlay, D21 OCaml `-loader.elf` + `-plugin.cmxs` (HCFG only in the plugin), D22 F# .NET\n10\t  (+ `FSharp.Core.dll` support member), D23 VB.NET (`sample.dll` + `runtimeconfig.json`), D24 Scala jar PAIR\n11\t  (`-vulnerable.jar` + `-corrected.jar`, 4 KB each), **D25 Clojure jar PAIR** (same role names, ~8 KB each).\n12\t  Since D18 each day = a structure/behaviour THEME on a new language: call graph (D18), packing (D19), resources/overlays (D20),\n13\t  shared libraries (D21), managed<->native bridge (D22), anti-analysis predicates (D23), PATCH DIFFING (D24: \"Two builds,\n14\t  one fix. Diff the vulnerable function against its corrected twin ... prove the old one was really broken\"), BOUNDS-ERROR ROOT\n15\t  CAUSE (D25: \"the code reaches where it shouldn't. Prove the bounds error is real, trace its reachability, and compare against\n16\t  the corrected twin\"). D24-D25 = a VULN-RESEARCH arc on vulnerable/corrected twins (null deref -> OOB read; next: another bug\n17\t  class -- integer overflow, UAF, format string, injection -- or a native twin). D22-D25 = \"new language on an old runtime\" 4x\n18\t  (F#, VB.NET, Scala, Clojure -- the predicted one): Groovy is the last obvious JVM language (d07 text still leaks \"Day 26 ...\n19\t  primary classfile named by that unit\"), then C++/CLI, Elixir/BEAM, Haxe->Neko.\n20\t  Ids `dNN_artifact_sha256_K` / `dNN_analysis_<field>`; multi-member groups add `dNN_analysis_<tag>_<field>` (D15/D16/D21) and\n21\t  D21 also had UNQUALIFIED ids whose QUESTION names the member.\n22\t- From D2 every new member embeds the **HCFG** blob `'HCFG' | u8 ver | u8 xor_key | u16le len | u32le crc32(plain) | xor'd JSON\n23\t  @12`; only its STORAGE changes (see Variant axes). Scan raw bytes for `HCFG` AND base64 `SENGR...`, crc-gate every hit; when\n24\t  both miss, look past the image end (overlay) and read the question -- it spells the unpacker. The JSON has never-asked keys\n25\t  too (ipv4, windows_path, linux_path, service, host_model): parse the whole dict.\n26\t- The analysis is easy; the hard part is the GM's label for `exact_text` fields. **The organizers RE-ISSUE the contract** when a\n27\t  label is unguessable (D17 `hcfg_storage` -> enum + ordered rules). Since D17 question texts are SPECS (D19 spelled the stub).\n28\t  `format` is `kind: enum` on d12+: `elf, pe, pe_cli, jar, wasm, neko_bytecode`.\n29\t- **The contract LEAKS future days**: D19 named \"RS20 for Day 20\" (came true). Still open after D24: enum `neko_bytecode`, d07\n30\t  `method_count` \"for Day 26 use the primary classfile named by that unit\". Grep each contract for `[A-Z]{2}\\d\\d`, `Day NN`,\n31\t  unseen enum values (D21-D24: nothing new).\n32\t- **Theme asked on its own group only sometimes**: D5-D18 never; D19 (`overlay_offset`/`overlay_size`), D20\n33\t  (`hcfg_resource_size`) yes; D21-D24 NO (D24: 2 sha256 + `<role>_format` + config_* x2). Imports/exports/dlopen/ImplMap/\n34\t  predicates/the D24 method diff = backfill candidates (D17 precedent).\n35\t- **Every member since D2 embeds a `huntress.binary.dynamic_trace.v1` template** (unasked) {branch, event_count, campaign, family\n36\t  `<lang>_<theme>_trace`, effects, network none} gated on env `HUNTRESS_HOST_MODEL` (analysis/sandbox/workstation). Recent\n37\t  family/effects: D20 `haskell_resource_overlay_trace`, D21 `ocaml_controlled_dynlink_trace`, D22 `fsharp_managed_native_bridge_\n38\t  trace`/`inert_native_process_id_bridge`, D23 `vbnet_anti_analysis_predicate_trace`/`inert_predicate_only` (branches `success`/\n39\t  `decoy`/`failure`, extra field `analysis_detected`), D24 `scala_patch_diff_trace`/`benign_control_and_reversion_only` (extra\n40\t  boolean `control_positive`).\n41\t- Question count: 80 on D8, +10/day to 160 (D16), D17 204 (backfill #2), then +12/day: D24 288, **D25 300**, no backfill since D17.\n42\t  Mastery = `setN.` copies (+1 set/day: D24 8 sets, **D25 9 sets = 2700 ids, ~36 MB per delivery**), artifacts `delivery N:\n43\t  evidence.zip`. Timed end to end: D22 12.3 / 18.2 s; D23 13.0 / 7.9 s; D24 5.0 / 8.4 s; **D25 TT 10.5 s; Mastery first POST\n44\t  54 s INCORRECT (55 ids cross-wired, see Pitfalls), CORRECT ~2 min after start via localize + a live worker.**\n45\t- **D24 contract re-wording (all groups)**: questions are now full SPECS -- sha256 \"Use all dNN-- members in ZIP central-directory\n46\t  order ... member K (1-based)\"; format lists every enum token with its rule; config questions spell the whole HCFG layout and\n47\t  the carrier rule per container (JAR: \"Base64-alphabet UTF-8 constants of at least 80 characters ... first CRC32-valid\").\n48\t\n49\t## Variant axes (what differs between the single, Time Trial and Mastery variants -- parse every value listed)\n50\t- **HCFG location / encoding** -- same blob, storage per container: `.hcfg` section (D2/D10/D14), .NET FieldRVA (D3), Go/Rust\n51\t  rodata, base64 in a jar constant pool (Java/Kotlin, D24 Scala `$` module `ldc`, D25 Clojure `<ns>__init.class` `ldc` for the\n52\t