ar, D7 Kotlin jar, D8 Swift (67 MB), D9 Nim, D10 Zig (PE in Mastery), D11 D, D12 Free Pascal, D13 Crystal,\n  D14 ObjC, D15 C pair `-stripped`/`-symbolized`, D16 WASM pair `-compact`/`-direct`, D17 Ada, D18 Fortran, D19 GnuCOBOL + `PK19`\n  packed overlay, D20 Haskell + `RS20` overlay, D21 OCaml `-loader.elf` + `-plugin.cmxs` (HCFG only in the plugin), D22 F# .NET\n  (+ `FSharp.Core.dll` support member), D23 VB.NET (`sample.dll` + `runtimeconfig.json`), D24 Scala jar PAIR\n  (`-vulnerable.jar` + `-corrected.jar`, 4 KB each), **D25 Clojure jar PAIR** (same role names, ~8 KB each).\n  Since D18 each day = a structure/behaviour THEME on a new language: call graph (D18), packing (D19), resources/overlays (D20),\n  shared libraries (D21), managed<->native bridge (D22), anti-analysis predicates (D23), PATCH DIFFING (D24: \"Two builds,\n  one fix. Diff the vulnerable function against its corrected twin ... prove the old one was really broken\"), BOUNDS-ERROR ROOT\n  CAUSE (D25: \"the code reaches where it shouldn't. Prove the bounds error is real, trace its reachability, and compare against\n  the corrected twin\"). D24-D25 = a VULN-RESEARCH arc on vulnerable/corrected twins (null deref -> OOB read; next: another bug\n  class -- integer overflow, UAF, format string, injection -- or a native twin). D22-D25 = \"new language on an old runtime\" 4x\n  (F#, VB.NET, Scala, Clojure -- the predicted one): Groovy is the last obvious JVM language (d07 text still leaks \"Day 26 ...\n  primary classfile named by that unit\"), then C++/CLI, Elixir/BEAM, Haxe->Neko.\n  Ids `dNN_artifact_sha256_K` / `dNN_analysis_<field>`; multi-member groups add `dNN_analysis_<tag>_<field>` (D15/D16/D21) and\n  D21 also had UNQUALIFIED ids whose QUESTION names the member.\n- From D2 every new member embeds the **HCFG** blob `'HCFG' | u8 ver | u8 xor_key | u16le len | u32le crc32(plain) | xor'd JSON\n  @12`; only its STORAGE changes (see Variant axes). Scan raw bytes for `HCFG` AND base64 `SENGR...`, crc