da / Fortran ELF (`NimMain`; `_D4core`; `Crystal:H`; `FPC 3.2.2`; `__objc_*`; `GNAT Version`; `libgfortran.so.5`) | Plain ELF (`elf`/`x86-64`/`62`), carried-over solver; HCFG base64 `SENGR...` (Nim/D/Crystal, offset = the `S`; Nim has raw decoys) or RAW (FPC `.data`, ObjC `.hcfg`, Ada/Fortran `.rodata`; offset = the `H`) |\n125\t| GnuCOBOL (`libcob.so.1`, `cob_init`) / Haskell GHC (`Main_main*_closure`, z-encoded `ghczminternal_*`, `GHC 9.x`) / OCaml (`caml_startup`, `camlStdlib__*`, `4.02.3`; `.cmxs` = natdynlink ET_DYN plugin, dynsyms `caml_plugin_header`, magic `Caml2007D002`) | Plain ELF for header ids; config NOT in the image for COBOL/Haskell (PK19/RS20 overlay past the section-header table, D19/D20); OCaml: HCFG RAW in the plugin `.data`; `nm -D --defined-only`, `readelf -dW` for exports/NEEDED |\n126\t| File size > `e_shoff + e_shnum*e_shentsize` (or > max section end), with or without a crc-valid HCFG | Appended OVERLAY: `xxd -s <image_end> F`; magic `<2 caps><day>` (`PK19` D19, `RS20` D20); parse the header fields the question lists, verify its bounds/sha256, run its transform if any, HCFG at the stated offset. A raw HCFG hit INSIDE the overlay (D20) still needs the header fields (`hcfg_resource_size`, offsets) |\n127\t| Two members differing by a name tag (D15/D16 builds, D21 loader+plugin), ids `dNN_analysis_<tag>_<field>` | Route each id to the member whose file name carries `<tag>`; UNqualified ids -> the member the QUESTION names; a role member (loader) may carry no HCFG |\n128\t| `00 61 73 6d 01 00 00 00` (`\\0asm`), `.wasm` | `lib.binary.wasm_layout(data)` or `wasm-objdump -x f.wasm`; format `wasm`, architecture `wasm32`; HCFG RAW in data segment 0 |\n129\t| `NEKO` magic / `.n` file (format enum lists `neko_bytecode` since D19) | Neko VM bytecode (Haxe/nekoc): `neko`/`haxe` are apt-installable; globals table holds the string constants -> HCFG scan; format `neko_bytecode` |\n130\t| `answer_format.kind: enum` + `accepted_values`, question says \"Apply