 **D19 \"Jack in the Box\"** (T+2:25): GnuCOBOL + `PK19` packed\n146\toverlay; NEW `overlay_offset`/`overlay_size`; the questions spelled the stub. **D20 \"Resourceful\"** (T+49 s): Haskell + `RS20`\n147\toverlay; NEW `hcfg_resource_size`. **D21 \"Shared Custody\"** (T+1:33): OCaml loader + `.cmxs` plugin; question-named member\n148\trouting AFTER the qualifier peel (running it first dropped 26 ids).\n149\t\n150\t**D22 \"Bridge Troll\"** (T+47 s): F# `sample.dll` + runtimeconfig + 5.7 MB `FSharp.Core.dll` support member; 2 P/Invoke ImplMap\n151\trows (unasked); HCFG RAW twice (\"FIRST record that validates\"); basenames renamed `variant-000` -> `sample`. **D23 \"Trust Issues\"**\n152\t(T+84 s, zero new code): VB.NET 8 KB, HCFG RAW only as the PE overlay; anti-analysis predicates UNASKED; timed modes re-shaped values.\n153\t**D24 \"Spot the Difference\"** (T+35 s, zero new code): Scala 2.13 twin jars `-vulnerable`/`-corrected`; only `score(String)I`\n154\tchanged (nonEmpty-then-charAt NPEs on null, CWE-476 -> `Option(s)...getOrElse(-1)`); 12 new ids = 2 sha256 + `<role>_format` +\n155\t4 unqualified \"both members must agree\" config_* + 4 `corrected_config_*`; HCFG base64 `ldc` in the `Foo$` module.\n156\t\n157\t**D25 \"Out of Bounds\"** (slug `synthetic-vulnerability-root-cause`; 300 Qs; **CORRECT T+80 s by the race harness's carried-over\n158\tsolver, 0 wrong, zero new code** -- ~69 s of it was the 36 MB download; TT 10.5 s first try; Mastery 9 sets see below).\n159\t- Artifact: new group `d25--sample-vulnerable.jar` (member 1, 8.3 KB) + `d25--sample-corrected.jar` (member 2, 8.4 KB), CLOJURE\n160\t  AOT jars (`Compiled from \"vulnerable000.clj\"`): `day25/<role>000.class` (gen-class Main stub), `<role>000__init.class` (ns\n161\t  loader: Vars `encoded-config` = base64 `SENGR...` ldc, `parse-frame`, `-main`), `<role>000$parse_frame.class`,\n162\t  `<role>000$_main.class`, `fn__269`, `loading__6812__auto____267`. clojure.jar not bundled; never executed.\n163\t- The bug (theme, UNASKED): `parse-frame` = `(nth frame 4)` -> `RT.nth(Object,int)` with NO bound -> IndexOutOfBoundsException\n164\t  on a short frame (CWE-125 OOB read / CWE-129 unchecked index); corrected = `(if (< 4 (count frame)) (nth frame 4) -1)`\n165\t  (`RT.count` + `lcmp`/`ifge` -> const `-1`). Reachability: `-main` reads `HUNTRESS_HOST_MODEL` (workstation...) and\n166\t  `HUNTRESS_TRIGGER_FAULT` == `\"1\"`, then picks a 2-element frame `[1 2]` (faults) or the 5-element `[1 2 3 4 5]`; trace family\n167\t  `clojure_bounds_root_cause_trace`, effects `bounded_synthetic_fault_only`. Found with `javap -p -c -constants` per class.\n168\t- 12 new ids, SAME shape and wording as D24 (2 sha256, `vulnerable_format`/`corrected_format` = `jar`, 4 unqualified consensus\n169\t  config_*, 4 `corrected_config_*`); JAR carrier rule \"Base64-alphabet UTF-8 constants >= 80 chars\" covered `__init.class`.\n170\t- Mastery (9 sets, 2700 ids): the daemon's first POST was INCORRECT -- 55 ids in 5 sets carried values of a DIFFERENT group of\n171\t  the same delivery (solver caches keyed on `id(member bytes)`, see Pitfalls); GM per-set feedback + localize fixed 9 label ids, a\n172\t  live worker re-derived the other 46 by a direct per-member HCFG scan (pyzipper `infected`) -> CORRECT ~2 min after start.\n173\t- Insight: the theme (\"prove the bounds error\", \"trace its reachability\") again asked only header + HCFG; the twin shape is now\n174\t  a template. The day's real risk was solver plumbing at 9 sets, not reversing.\n175\t\n176\t## GM answer conventions learned\n177\t| Field family | Accepted form | Rejected (never resubmit) |\n178\t|---|---|---|\n179\t| elf_class (`kind` exact_text) | `ELF64` / `ELF32` (readelf style) | ELFCLASS64 |\n180\t| elf_class (`kind: integer`, D8) | the bit width `64` / `32` | `2` / `1` (raw EI_CLASS byte) |\n181\t| machine (`kind: integer`, D8-D9, D15, D21 loader/plugin) | decimal e_machine (`62` = x86-64), also for an ET_DYN `.cmxs` | — |\n182\t| endian