{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgP1owozrWwNskkw3jekr","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_0156QBM8ggWfAMuNnf2kDdwG","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /home/testpwn/huntress-2026; python3 - <<'EOF'\nimport json,re\np=\"reference/coverage/binary-reverse-engineering.md\"\ns=open(p).read()\nm=re.search(r\"(## Readiness gaps\\n```json\\n)(.*?)(\\n```)\",s,re.S)\ngaps=json.loads(m.group(2))\nby={g[\"id\"]:g for g in gaps}\ndef upd(i,**kw): by[i].update(kw)\n# built p1 items related to the twin arc: keep, annotate, demote\nupd(\"jvm-method-patch-diff-facts\", priority=2, detail=\"BUILT (prebuild-state ok). \"+by[\"jvm-method-patch-diff-facts\"][\"detail\"]+\" D25 re-used the shape on Clojure twins (only `parse-frame` changed) -- see jvm-twin-diff-gensym-normalization for the non-Scala naming.\")\nupd(\"vulnerability-trigger-proof\", priority=2, detail=\"BUILT (prebuild-state ok). \"+by[\"vulnerability-trigger-proof\"][\"detail\"]+\" D25 (seen, unasked): Clojure `RT.nth(v,4)` on the 2-element frame `[1 2]` -> java.lang.IndexOutOfBoundsException vs corrected -1; extend the stub model with clojure.lang.RT.nth/count/intCast, Util.equiv, Tuple.create.\")\nupd(\"vulnerability-class-classifier\", priority=2, detail=\"BUILT (prebuild-state ok). \"+by[\"vulnerability-class-classifier\"][\"detail\"]+\" D25 fixture = CWE-125 (unchecked index; CWE-129 also plausible): added `(< idx (count v))` guard before nth.\")\nupd(\"native-function-patch-diff\", priority=2, detail=\"BUILT (prebuild-state ok). \"+by[\"native-function-patch-diff\"][\"detail\"])\nupd(\"scala-module-class-facts\", priority=2, detail=\"BUILT (prebuild-state ok). \"+by[\"scala-module-class-facts\"][\"detail\"])\nupd(\"crash-exploitability-facts\", priority=1)\nupd(\"symbolic-input-solver\", priority=1, detail=by[\"symbolic-input-solver\"][\"detail\"]+\" D25 'trace its reachability' = which env values reach the bug: include the D25 Clojure `-main` (HUNTRESS_HOST_MODEL / HUNTRESS_TRIGGER_FAULT compares) as a fixture.\")\nupd(\"managed-patch-diff-dotnet\", detail=by[\"managed-patch-diff-dotnet\"][\"detail\"]+\" 1st attempt killed rc -9 with nothing written: scope to a pure-Python IL byte diff over two hand-patched copies of the cached D23 dll; no dotnet build.\")\nupd(\"stripped-twin-function-matching\", detail=by[\"stripped-twin-function-matching\"][\"detail\"]+\" 1st attempt killed rc -9 with nothing written: keep it to .eh_frame FDE ranges + normalised-instruction hashes with capstone; no angr/Ghidra.\")\nupd(\"theme-facts-recording\", detail=by[\"theme-facts-recording\"][\"detail\"]+\" d25: Clojure twins, changed fn `parse-frame` only (class `day25.<role>000$parse_frame`), vulnerable `(nth frame 4)` -> RT.nth(Object,int) IndexOutOfBoundsException on a short frame (CWE-125/129), corrected `(if (< 4 (count frame)) (nth frame 4) -1)`, `-main` gate HUNTRESS_HOST_MODEL (workstation) + HUNTRESS_TRIGGER_FAULT==\\\"1\\\" -> frame [1 2] vs [1 2 3 4 5], trace clojure_bounds_root_cause_trace / bounded_synthetic_fault_only, HCFG base64 in `<role>000__init.class` (Var encoded-config).\")\nupd(\"contract-forward-hints\", detail=by[\"contract-forward-hints\"][\"detail\"]+\" D25: no new token/day; d25 ids copy the D24 wording verbatim; Day 26 + neko_bytecode still open (Clojure's `__init` vs gen-class stub is a 2nd example of 'primary classfile named by that unit').\")\nupd(\"member-basename-vocabulary\", detail=by[\"member-basename-vocabulary\"][\"detail\"]+\" D25 timed modes added domain/url words edge/cache/vault/proxy/node and path words vault/edge/stage/sync/gate; url host word independent of the domain word.\")\nnew=[\n {\"id\":\"solver-member-cache-identity\",\"concept\":\"Per-member caches in the cumulative solver keyed on id(bytes) cross-wire members once Python reuses a freed object's address (D25 Mastery: 55 ids in 5/9 sets answered with another dNN-- group's facts)\",\"priority\":1,\"action\":\"note\",\"detail\":\"challenges/day25/binary-out-of-bounds/solver/solve.py keys _SHA/_ZIPS/_ISJAR/_FACTS/_CFG on id(b) (lines ~61-126, 303-317, 692, 872-891); with 9 sets x ~34 members the first daemon POST failed (d23 <- d03 config, d22/d15 <- d10 PE header, d06/d24 <- d16 wasm, d25 vulnerable <- d03 pe_cli). Fix before D26's timed modes: key on (delivery path, member name) or sha256, or hold every member's bytes in a list for the run; add a regression that runs a 9-set Mastery case (cases/variant-mastery-f395c0c5) with HCTF_SOLVER_PARALLEL=0 and =1. Diagnostic rule: a rejected value that is a VALID answer for a different group of the same delivery = routing/cache bug, not a label problem.\"},\n {\"id\":\"clojure-namespace-facts\",\"concept\":\"Clojure AOT jar identity facts for a d25 backfill: namespace, Var names in definition order, fn class per Var (`<ns>$<munged>`), `__init` class, gen-class Main stub, source file, Clojure compiler hints\",\"priority\":1,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\"detail\":\"Fixtures: the cached D25 jars (challenges/day25/binary-out-of-bounds/single_solve/work/extracted/evidence/d25--sample-{vulnerable,corrected}.jar). lib.binary.clojure_facts(jar): namespace from `in-ns` / `RT.var(\\\"<ns>\\\",\\\"<name>\\\")` ldc pairs in `<ns>__init.class` (`day25.vulnerable000`; Vars encoded-config, parse-frame, -main in order), demunge class names (`_` -> `-`, `_main` -> `-main`, `$fn__NNN` anonymous, `loading__NNNN__auto____NNN` ns loader), per-fn invokeStatic arity, SourceFile (`vulnerable000.clj`), primary_class (the class holding the HCFG ldc = `__init`), main_class (manifest), has_clojure_runtime (refs to clojure/lang/ while clojure.jar is NOT bundled), Var metadata (:line/:column/:file, :arglists `[frame]`). Expose as facts keys (namespace, vars, fn_classes, primary_class, source_file) for unknown d25 ids.\"},\n {\"id\":\"groovy-script-class-facts\",\"concept\":\"Groovy compiled member (groovyc script or class) -- the last obvious JVM language and the best fit for the d07 'Day 26 ... primary classfile named by that unit' leak\",\"priority\":1,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\"detail\":\"Cues: superclass groovy/lang/Script (script) or GroovyObject impl, synthetic $getStaticMetaClass/$getCallSiteArray/$createCallSiteArray, CallSite invocations, closures `<Unit>$_run_closure1`/`$_main_closure1` extending groovy/lang/Closure with doCall, SourceFile `<Unit>.groovy`, refs org/codehaus/groovy/runtime/ (groovy jar NOT bundled, as Scala/Clojure). 'Primary classfile named by that unit' = the class whose name / SourceFile stem equals the unit, not closures or the manifest. Facts: primary_class, closures (table order), methods/method_count/access_flags of the primary class (the d07 field family), string constants via CallSite args, HCFG base64 in the primary class constant pool. Fixtures: if `groovyc` is not installable, synthesize classfiles with the D06 jar writer using those names/superclasses + an HCFG ldc; test that jar_hcfg + method facts route to the unit-named class.\"},\n {\"id\":\"bug-reachability-gating-facts\",\"concept\":\"'Trace its reachability': the call path from the entry point to the vulnerable call and the input/env predicates that must hold (env var names + compared values, argv/stdin/file checks), per member and per host model\",\"priority\":1,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\"detail\":\"D25 (unasked): Clojure `-main` -> System.getenv(HUNTRESS_HOST_MODEL) compared to `workstation`, getenv(HUNTRESS_TRIGGER_FAULT) Util.equiv \\\"1\\\" -> chooses frame const__3 [1 2] (2 elements) vs const__7 [1 2 3 4 5] -> parse-frame (nth 4). Build lib.binary.reachability_facts(member, target_fn): JVM -- walk invokeStatic/IFn.invoke edges from main/-main (resolve Var.getRawRoot of `RT.var` names to fn classes), collect the getenv/equals/equiv/lookupswitch predicates on the path and the constant collections (Tuple.create arity / array sizes) fed to the target; native -- capstone call graph (prebuilt callgraph-indirect-flow-facts) + getenv/strcmp/argv compares before the call. Output: call_path (JSON names), gate_env_vars (JSON, order of use), gate_values, trigger_condition text, reachable_for_<host_model> booleans, input_size_on_trigger (2) vs safe (5). Fixtures: D25 jars + D24 jars + a C twin with getenv-gated memcpy.\"},\n {\"id\":\"jvm-twin-diff-gensym-normalization\",\"concept\":\"JVM twin diff across languages whose class/method names embed role tokens and compiler gensyms (Clojure `fn__269`, `loading__6812__auto____267`; Kotlin `$lambda$0`, Scala `$anonfun$score$1`, Groovy `_closure1`): normalise before matching\",\"priority\":1,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\"detail\":\"The built jvm-method-patch-diff-facts matched Scala `Day24<Role>000$`; D25's Clojure twins name classes `day25/<role>000$parse_frame` and share gensym numbers only by accident. Normalise: strip the role token (vulnerable/corrected/patched/fixed/old/new) from package+class names, map gensym suffixes by position/Var name, resolve constant-pool operands to symbolic strings, ignore LineNumberTable/LocalVariableTable/StackMapTable and SourceFile; for Clojure compare per-Var fn classes (`$parse_frame` invokeStatic bytecode). Report changed_vars / changed_methods, guard instructions added (RT.count + lcmp/ifge, ifnull, Option$), constants added (-1). Fixtures: D24 + D25 cached jars (expected: only score / only parse-frame changed).\"},\n {\"id\":\"native-bounds-check-twins\",\"concept\":\"Native OOB twin pairs and language bounds-check signatures: C manual `cmp idx,len; jae` inserted, `-fsanitize=bounds` `__ubsan_handle_out_of_bounds`, Rust `core::panicking::panic_bounds_check` / `slice_index_len_fail`, Go `runtime.panicIndex`/`panicSlice*`, Swift `Fatal error: Index out of range`, FORTIFY `__memcpy_chk`\",\"priority\":2,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\"detail\":\"If the bounds theme moves to native twins: lib.binary.bounds_check_facts(a, b) on top of the built native-function-patch-diff -- per function count of bounds-check calls/compares, the index constant and buffer length (lea/sub rsp, array size from .rodata), unchecked accesses (mov reg, [base+idx*scale] with no dominating cmp), and which twin adds the check. Fixtures: gcc C pair (array[idx] vs if (idx < N)), Rust-shaped symbols synthetic (no cargo), Go-shaped `runtime.panicIndex` call synthetic; expected facts for each.\"},\n {\"id\":\"next-bug-class-twin-fixtures\",\"concept\":\"Fixture twins for the bug classes not yet shipped (integer overflow/signedness, UAF/double free, format string, command/SQL injection, unsafe deserialization, path traversal, TOCTOU, uninitialised read) across JVM, .NET and native, so the classifier/diff/trigger tools are tested before the day lands\",\"priority\":2,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\"detail\":\"Arc: D24 null deref (CWE-476), D25 OOB read (CWE-125) -- one class per day on vulnerable/corrected twins. Build tests/data twin pairs: javac (Math.addExact vs +; Runtime.exec with/without allow-list; ObjectInputStream with/without filter; File canonical path check), C via gcc (size_t wrap before malloc; free then use vs free+NULL; printf(user) vs printf(\\\"%s\\\"); signed len compare), each with the HUNTRESS-style getenv gate and an HCFG blob. For each, record expected changed function, CWE token, trigger input, outcome per build, and run the built vulnerability-class-classifier/vulnerability-trigger-proof against them (fix gaps they reveal).\"},\n {\"id\":\"standalone-classfile-member\",\"concept\":\"A bare `.class` member (CAFEBABE, no zip) or a multi-class jar without a usable Main-Class: format label, primary class selection 'named by that unit', HCFG in its constant pool\",\"priority\":2,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\"detail\":\"d07 method_count text: 'for Day 26 use the primary classfile named by that unit'. The format enum has no `class` token (elf, pe, pe_cli, jar, wasm, neko_bytecode) -> a lone classfile may still be `jar`-family or the enum grows: read accepted_values. Distinguish from Mach-O FAT (cafebabe + small nfat_arch) by major_version >= 45 at +6. Solver: magic dispatch for CAFEBABE, constant-pool base64 HCFG scan (same carrier rule as JAR), methods/method_count/access_flags from that class; primary class = name or SourceFile stem matching the unit the question names. Fixtures: javac single class + a 3-class jar without Main-Class.\"}\n]\nfor g in new:\n    assert g[\"id\"] not in by\ngaps=[by[g[\"id\"]] for g in gaps]\n# insert new gaps: p1 ones at top, p2 ones after the last p1\np1=[g for g in new if g[\"priority\"]==1]; p2=[g for g in new if g[\"priority\"]==2]\ngaps=p1+gaps\n# stable-sort by priority\ngaps=sorted(gaps,key=lambda g:g[\"priority\"])\nidx=max(i for i,g in enumerate(gaps) if g[\"priority\"]==2)\ngaps=gaps[:idx+1]+p2+gaps[idx+1:] if False else gaps\n# place p2 new right after p1 block\nfirst2=next(i for i,g in enumerate(gaps) if g[\"priority\"]==2)\ngaps=gaps[:first2]+p2+gaps[first2:]\nbody=\"[\\n\"+\",\\n\".join(\"  \"+json.dumps(g,ensure_ascii=False) for g in gaps)+\"\\n]\"\njson.loads(body)\ns=s[:m.start(2)]+body+s[m.end(2):]\nopen(p,\"w\").write(s)\nst=json.load(open(\".run/prebuild-state.json\"))\npend=[g[\"id\"] for g in gaps if g[\"action\"]==\"prebuild\" and not ((v:=st.get(\"binary-reverse-engineering:\"+g[\"id\"])) and (v.get(\"ok\") or v.get(\"attempts\",0)>=2))]\nprint(len(gaps), len(pend), pend)\nprint([ (g[\"id\"],g[\"priority\"]) for g in gaps if g[\"priority\"]==1])\nEOF"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1379,"cache_read_input_tokens":215943,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1379},"output_tokens":6,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e7b9f74d-13fa-4643-a706-3e89af5c6241","uuid":"c1ad102c-6cdc-4b74-95e9-a2ab4862471d","timestamp":"2026-10-25T13:14:32.702Z","request_id":"req_011CgP1owMU8e1DsFdGJt1Uy","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_0156QBM8ggWfAMuNnf2kDdwG":{"command":"cd /home/testpwn/huntress-2026; python3 - <<'EOF'\nimport json,re\np=\"reference/coverage/binary-reverse-engineering.md\"\ns=open(p).read()\nm=re.search(r\"(## Readiness gaps\\n```json\\n)(.*?)(\\n```)\",s,re.S)\ngaps=json.loads(m.group(2))\nby={g[\"id\"]:g for g in gaps}\ndef upd(i,**kw): by[i].update(kw)\n# built p1 items related to the twin arc: keep, annotate, demote\nupd(\"jvm-method-patch-diff-facts\", priority=2, detail=\"BUILT (prebuild-state ok). \"+by[\"jvm-method-patch-diff-facts\"][\"detail\"]+\" D25 re-used the shape on Clojure twins (only `parse-frame` changed) -- see jvm-twin-diff-gensym-normalization for the non-Scala naming.\")\nupd(\"vulnerability-trigger-proof\", priority=2, detail=\"BUILT (prebuild-state ok). \"+by[\"vulnerability-trigger-proof\"][\"detail\"]+\" D25 (seen, unasked): Clojure `RT.nth(v,4)` on the 2-element frame `[1 2]` -> java.lang.IndexOutOfBoundsException vs corrected -1; extend the stub model with clojure.lang.RT.nth/count/intCast, Util.equiv, Tuple.create.\")\nupd(\"vulnerability-class-classifier\", priority=2, detail=\"BUILT (prebuild-state ok). \"+by[\"vulnerability-class-classifier\"][\"detail\"]+\" D25 fixture = CWE-125 (unchecked index; CWE-129 also plausible): added `(< idx (count v))` guard before nth.\")\nupd(\"native-function-patch-diff\", priority=2, detail=\"BUILT (prebuild-state ok). \"+by[\"native-function-patch-diff\"][\"detail\"])\nupd(\"scala-module-class-facts\", priority=2, detail=\"BUILT (prebuild-state ok). \"+by[\"scala-module-class-facts\"][\"detail\"])\nupd(\"crash-exploitability-facts\", priority=1)\nupd(\"symbolic-input-solver\", priority=1, detail=by[\"symbolic-input-solver\"][\"detail\"]+\" D25 'trace its reachability' = which env values reach the bug: include the D25 Clojure `-main` (HUNTRESS_HOST_MODEL / HUNTRESS_TRIGGER_FAULT compares) as a fixture.\")\nupd(\"managed-patch-diff-dotnet\", detail=by[\"managed-patch-diff-dotnet\"][\"detail\"]+\" 1st attempt killed rc -9 with nothing written: scope to a pure-Python IL byte diff over two hand-patched copies of the cached D23 dll; no dotnet build.\")\nupd(\"stripped-twin-function-matching\", detail=by[\"stripped-twin-function-matching\"][\"detail\"]+\" 1st attempt killed rc -9 with nothing written: keep it to .eh_frame FDE ranges + normalised-instruction hashes with capstone; no angr/Ghidra.\")\nupd(\"theme-facts-recording\", detail=by[\"theme-facts-recording\"][\"detail\"]+\" d25: Clojure twins, changed fn `parse-frame` only (class `day25.<role>000$parse_frame`), vulnerable `(nth frame 4)` -> RT.nth(Object,int) IndexOutOfBoundsException on a short frame (CWE-125/129), corrected `(if (< 4 (count frame)) (nth frame 4) -1)`, `-main` gate HUNTRESS_HOST_MODEL (workstation) + HUNTRESS_TRIGGER_FAULT==\\\"1\\\" -> frame [1 2] vs [1 2 3 4 5], trace clojure_bounds_root_cause_trace / bounded_synthetic_fault_only, HCFG base64 in `<role>000__init.class` (Var encoded-config).\")\nupd(\"contract-forward-hints\", detail=by[\"contract-forward-hints\"][\"detail\"]+\" D25: no new token/day; d25 ids copy the D24 wording verbatim; Day 26 + neko_bytecode still open (Clojure's `__init` vs gen-class stub is a 2nd example of 'primary classfile named by that unit').\")\nupd(\"member-basename-vocabulary\", detail=by[\"member-basename-vocabulary\"][\"detail\"]+\" D25 timed modes added domain/url words edge/cache/vault/proxy/node and path words vault/edge/stage/sync/gate; url host word independent of the domain word.\")\nnew=[\n {\"id\":\"solver-member-cache-identity\",\"concept\":\"Per-member caches in the cumulative solver keyed on id(bytes) cross-wire members once Python reuses a freed object's address (D25 Mastery: 55 ids in 5/9 sets answered with another dNN-- group's facts)\",\"priority\":1,\"action\":\"note\",\"detail\":\"challenges/day25/binary-out-of-bounds/solver/solve.py keys _SHA/_ZIPS/_ISJAR/_FACTS/_CFG on id(b) (lines ~61-126, 303-317, 692, 872-891); with 9 sets x ~34 members the first daemon POST failed (d23 <- d03 config, d22/d15 <- d10 PE header, d06/d24 <- d16 wasm, d25 vulnerable <- d03 pe_cli). Fix before D26's timed modes: key on (delivery path, member name) or sha256, or hold every member's bytes in a list for the run; add a regression that runs a 9-set Mastery case (cases/variant-mastery-f395c0c5) with HCTF_SOLVER_PARALLEL=0 and =1. Diagnostic rule: a rejected value that is a VALID answer for a different group of the same delivery = routing/cache bug, not a label problem.\"},\n {\"id\":\"clojure-namespace-facts\",\"concept\":\"Clojure AOT jar identity facts for a d25 backfill: namespace, Var names in definition order, fn class per Var (`<ns>$<munged>`), `__init` class, gen-class Main stub, source file, Clojure compiler hints\",\"priority\":1,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\"detail\":\"Fixtures: the cached D25 jars (challenges/day25/binary-out-of-bounds/single_solve/work/extracted/evidence/d25--sample-{vulnerable,corrected}.jar). lib.binary.clojure_facts(jar): namespace from `in-ns` / `RT.var(\\\"<ns>\\\",\\\"<name>\\\")` ldc pairs in `<ns>__init.class` (`day25.vulnerable000`; Vars encoded-config, parse-frame, -main in order), demunge class names (`_` -> `-`, `_main` -> `-main`, `$fn__NNN` anonymous, `loading__NNNN__auto____NNN` ns loader), per-fn invokeStatic arity, SourceFile (`vulnerable000.clj`), primary_class (the class holding the HCFG ldc = `__init`), main_class (manifest), has_clojure_runtime (refs to clojure/lang/ while clojure.jar is NOT bundled), Var metadata (:line/:column/:file, :arglists `[frame]`). Expose as facts keys (namespace, vars, fn_classes, primary_class, source_file) for unknown d25 ids.\"},\n {\"id\":\"groovy-script-class-facts\",\"concept\":\"Groovy compiled member (groovyc script or class) -- the last obvious JVM language and the best fit for the d07 'Day 26 ... primary classfile named by that unit' leak\",\"priority\":1,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\"detail\":\"Cues: superclass groovy/lang/Script (script) or GroovyObject impl, synthetic $getStaticMetaClass/$getCallSiteArray/$createCallSiteArray, CallSite invocations, closures `<Unit>$_run_closure1`/`$_main_closure1` extending groovy/lang/Closure with doCall, SourceFile `<Unit>.groovy`, refs org/codehaus/groovy/runtime/ (groovy jar NOT bundled, as Scala/Clojure). 'Primary classfile named by that unit' = the class whose name / SourceFile stem equals the unit, not closures or the manifest. Facts: primary_class, closures (table order), methods/method_count/access_flags of the primary class (the d07 field family), string constants via CallSite args, HCFG base64 in the primary class constant pool. Fixtures: if `groovyc` is not installable, synthesize classfiles with the D06 jar writer using those names/superclasses + an HCFG ldc; test that jar_hcfg + method facts route to the unit-named class.\"},\n {\"id\":\"bug-reachability-gating-facts\",\"concept\":\"'Trace its reachability': the call path from the entry point to the vulnerable call and the input/env predicates that must hold (env var names + compared values, argv/stdin/file checks), per member and per host model\",\"priority\":1,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\"detail\":\"D25 (unasked): Clojure `-main` -> System.getenv(HUNTRESS_HOST_MODEL) compared to `workstation`, getenv(HUNTRESS_TRIGGER_FAULT) Util.equiv \\\"1\\\" -> chooses frame const__3 [1 2] (2 elements) vs const__7 [1 2 3 4 5] -> parse-frame (nth 4). Build lib.binary.reachability_facts(member, target_fn): JVM -- walk invokeStatic/IFn.invoke edges from main/-main (resolve Var.getRawRoot of `RT.var` names to fn classes), collect the getenv/equals/equiv/lookupswitch predicates on the path and the constant collections (Tuple.create arity / array sizes) fed to the target; native -- capstone call graph (prebuilt callgraph-indirect-flow-facts) + getenv/strcmp/argv compares before the call. Output: call_path (JSON names), gate_env_vars (JSON, order of us